{"parentUuid":"34ba4dcb-28c0-4fca-958e-36c5f79256f0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e730da08-9269-40a3-baa4-8d9f7a66c317","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C9SD246Wjz3ZWWd4fU7VcB","type":"tool_result","content":"\"content\":\"can you see untracked changes in this branch\"\n\"content\":\"?? cmd/entire-activity-demo/\\n?? docs/2026-04-15-entire-activity-design.md\"\n\"content\":\"yes, and we've done chunk 1 and we were well into track 2, but we shut down, so can you see where we are, or use entire skill to see if you can recover the session, i can't find it\"\n\"content\":\"Launching skill: entire:session-handoff\"\n\"content\":\"● Enabled · manual-commit · branch entire-activity\\n  Agents · Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode\\n\\n── Active Sessions ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nClaude Code · ec8f3ded-6e61-4f61-906d-1d42e68db462\\n> \\\"\n\"content\":\"No files found\"\n\"content\":\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.git\"\n\"content\":\"1\\t# Entire Activity Design\\n2\\t\\n3\\tDate: 2026-04-15 (revised 2026-04-16)\\n4\\t\\n5\\t## Summary\\n6\\t\\n7\\t`entire activity` is a new read-only product surface for understanding work captured by Entire over time.\\n8\\t\\n9\\tIt is centered on:\\n10\\t\\n11\\t- **sessions** as the primary unit of work\\n12\\t- **checkpoints** as the evidence trail inside a session\\n13\\t- **repo, time, and agent** as first-class grouping dimensions\\n14\\t\\n15\\tThis is not a sprint tool and should not use sprint language. It is an Entire-native activity layer over existing session, checkpoint, transcript, and commit-linkage data — rendered as a tabbed dashboard in the terminal.\\n16\\t\\n17\\t## Goals\\n18\\t\\n19\\t- Show what happened today and across selectable time ranges.\\n20\\t- Make checkpoint and session activity easy to scan quickly.\\n21\\t- Surface useful, defensible insights instead of generic churn metrics.\\n22\\t- Support today / range / history / agents / repos / report tabs in v1.\\n23\\t- Support interactive TUI and static output in v1.\\n24\\t- Use only metrics that are directly available now or safely derivable from existing data.\\n25\\t- Reuse existing CLI infrastructure (session state, checkpoint store, auth, lipgloss styles) rather than duplicating it.\\n26\\t\\n27\\t## Non-Goals\\n28\\t\\n29\\t- No productivity score.\\n30\\t- No “most modified files” leaderboard as a primary signal.\\n31\\t- No sprint framing.\\n32\\t- No LLM-generated prose in the CLI. (Server-side LLM classification is consumed as data, not re-generated locally.)\\n33\\t- No claims of labor time or focus time beyond actual timestamp spans.\\n34\\t- No local reimplementation of the server-side checkpoint analysis pipeline.\\n35\\t\\n36\\t## Product Definition\\n37\\t\\n38\\t`entire activity` answers:\\n39\\t\\n40\\t- what happened\\n41\\t- when it happened\\n42\\t- where it happened\\n43\\t- what kind of work it was\\n44\\t- which agents and models were involved\\n45\\t- which checkpoints linked to commits\\n46\\t- what should likely be resumed or finished\\n47\\t\\n48\\t## Information Architecture\\n49\\t\\n50\\tThe v1 surface is a **tabbed dashboard**. Six top-level tabs:\\n51\\t\\n52\\t```\\n53\\ttoday │ range │ history │ agents │ repos │ report\\n54\\t```\\n55\\t\\n56\\tRules:\\n57\\t\\n58\\t- Each tab is a self-contained view with its own panel layout. Panels never span tabs.\\n59\\t- Active tab is visually distinct (amber `214` with an underline rule); inactive tabs are faint gray `244`.\\n60\\t- Keyboard: `1-6` jump directly to a tab. `tab` / `shift-tab` cycle. `q` quits.\\n61\\t- Within a tab, arrow keys move between panels/rows. `enter` opens drill-down. `esc` closes drill-down.\\n62\\t- CLI subcommands map 1:1 to tabs: `entire activity today` opens the today tab, `entire activity agents` opens agents tab, etc.\\n63\\t\\n64\\tProfiles only change defaults and emphasis (heatmap metric, whether token panels are prominent, etc.):\\n65\\t\\n66\\t- `personal` (default)\\n67\\t- `team`\\n68\\t- `observability`\\n69\\t\\n70\\t## Command Surface\\n71\\t\\n72\\t```bash\\n73\\tentire activity                                 # opens TUI on 'today' tab\\n74\\tentire activity today\\n75\\tentire activity range --last 7d\\n76\\tentire activity range --from 2026-04-01 --to 2026-04-15\\n77\\tentire activity history\\n78\\tentire activity agents\\n79\\tentire activity repos\\n80\\tentire activity report --template daily --format markdown\"\n\"content\":\"# Entire Activity Design\\n\\nDate: 2026-04-15 (revised 2026-04-16)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n`entire activity` is a new read-only product surface for understanding work captured by Entire over time.\\n\\nIt is centered on:\\n\\n- **sessions** as the primary unit of work\\n- **checkpoints** as the evidence trail inside a session\\n- **repo, time, and agent** as first-class grouping dimensions\\n\\nThis is not a sprint tool and should not use sprint language. It is an Entire-native activity layer over existing session, checkpoint, transcript, and commit-linkage data — rendered as a tabbed dashboard in the terminal.\\n\\n## Goals\\n\\n- Show what happened today and across selectable time ranges.\\n- Make checkpoint and session activity easy to scan quickly.\\n- Surface useful, defensible insights instead of generic churn metrics.\\n- Support today / range / history / agents / repos / report tabs in v1.\\n- Support interactive TUI and static output in v1.\\n- Use only metrics that are directly available now or safely derivable from existing data.\\n- Reuse existing CLI infrastructure (session state, checkpoint store, auth, lipgloss styles) rather than duplicating it.\\n\\n## Non-Goals\\n\\n- No productivity score.\\n- No “most modified files” leaderboard as a primary signal.\\n- No sprint framing.\\n- No LLM-generated prose in the CLI. (Server-side LLM classification is consumed as data, not re-generated locally.)\\n- No claims of labor time or focus time beyond actual timestamp spans.\\n- No local reimplementation of the server-side checkpoint analysis pipeline.\\n\\n## Product Definition\\n\\n`entire activity` answers:\\n\\n- what happened\\n- when it happened\\n- where it happened\\n- what kind of work it was\\n- which agents and models were involved\\n- which checkpoints linked to commits\\n- what should likely be resumed or finished\\n\\n## Information Architecture\\n\\nThe v1 surface is a **tabbed dashboard**. Six top-level tabs:\\n\\n```\\ntoday │ range │ history │ agents │ repos │ report\\n```\\n\\nRules:\\n\\n- Each tab is a self-contained view with its own panel layout. Panels never span tabs.\\n- Active tab is visually distinct (amber `214` with an underline rule); inactive tabs are faint gray `244`.\\n- Keyboard: `1-6` jump directly to a tab. `tab` / `shift-tab` cycle. `q` quits.\\n- Within a tab, arrow keys move between panels/rows. `enter` opens drill-down. `esc` closes drill-down.\\n- CLI subcommands map 1:1 to tabs: `entire activity today` opens the today tab, `entire activity agents` opens agents tab, etc.\\n\\nProfiles only change defaults and emphasis (heatmap metric, whether token panels are prominent, etc.):\\n\\n- `personal` (default)\\n- `team`\\n- `observability`\\n\\n## Command Surface\\n\\n```bash\\nentire activity                                 # opens TUI on 'today' tab\\nentire activity today\\nentire activity range --last 7d\\nentire activity range --from 2026-04-01 --to 2026-04-15\\nentire activity history\\nentire activity agents\\nentire activity repos\\nentire activity report --template daily --format markdown\"\n\"content\":\"019d783b-5901-7592-b09d-ce70710faeaa.json\\n019d783b-5901-7592-b09d-ce70710faeaa.model\\n019d8d45-8274-7e22-a1f1-f94f13acfda4.json\\n019d8d73-b5a7-72a0-a7b0-6da0909d0518.json\\n019d8d73-b5a7-72a0-a7b0-6da0909d0518.model\\n019d9268-7c7a-7f32-85ae-5a574b0f4a3e.json\\n019d9268-7c7a-7f32-85ae-5a574b0f4a3e.model\\n019d9366-693d-76d1-a582-cc06158335a9.js