{"parentUuid":"91f166f9-d932-40a4-aa64-ffeebe148256","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GeQgt7FoDWsLyqLnmQ1CmT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JzdxexK8BmHAWvcvqdMX2g","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-21-entire-activity.md","content":"# Entire Activity Implementation Plan (v2)\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Ship `entire activity`: a terminal-native view over existing server checkpoint analyses + local session state, with three tabs (Day / Week / Agents) and a time-range toggle.\n\n**Architecture:** The CLI does not derive new metrics. It retrieves data that already exists (server `CheckpointAnalysis`, local `session.State`, `Entire-Checkpoint` commit trailers), aggregates it across a time range, and renders it in the terminal. All computation is simple grouping + summing — no transcript walking, no local classification, no tool-time derivation.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, `cobra` (commands), `bubbletea` + `lipgloss` (TUI), existing `activity` package (projections, loaders, heatmap, metrics), existing `api` client (enrichment).\n\n**Supersedes:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-15-entire-activity-v1-local-derivation.md` — original premise assumed local tool-time derivation. Server-side checkpoint analysis (labels + toolProfile + skills + agents + tokens) is now the authoritative source.\n\n---\n\n## Premise and scope\n\n**Data the CLI aggregates (already produced elsewhere):**\n\n| Source | Data |\n|---|---|\n| Server `CheckpointAnalysis` | labels, toolProfile, skillsUsed, mcpServersUsed, agentsUsed, modelsUsed, token totals |\n| Local `session.State` | agent, timestamps, files touched, checkpoints, session-level token usage |\n| Git (`Entire-Checkpoint` trailer) | checkpoint → commit linkage |\n\n**Out of scope for v1:**\n- Local tool-time derivation (walker, categorizer, `DeriveToolTime`) — server owns this\n- Focus-area rule engine — server labels cover intent classification\n- History / Repos / Report tabs — not in v1\n- Profiles (personal / team / observability) — keep it one default view\n- Multi-agent transcript parsing — only matters if CLI derives, which it doesn't\n\n**Optional / future:** export (markdown or JSON) — revisit after v1 ships.\n\n---\n\n## Tabs\n\n### Day tab\nToday's activity. One row per session started/active today. Per row: agent, time span, label(s), checkpoint count, commits produced, token usage.\n\n### Week tab\nLast 7 days. Top panel: per-day activity strip (reuse existing heatmap bucketing). Bottom panel: daily breakdown (same columns as Day) collapsed by day.\n\n### Agents tab\nPer-agent rollup with a **time-range toggle: `day | week | month | 30d | 90d`**.\nPer agent: session count, total checkpoints, tokens, dominant labels, top skills, top MCP servers. This is the only tab with the toggle; Day and Week are fixed ranges.\n\n---\n\n## Pre-work: revert + audit\n\n## Chunk R: Revert local derivation + audit Chunk 1\n\n- [ ] **Task R.1: Revert the walker stack**\n\nRevert 7 commits in order: `7560cd233`, `be94737c1`, `d030ac6c5`, `6113bdc42`, `646625fc3`, `3752d6c0d`, `59f61e35d`. Use `git revert --no-commit 7560cd233^..59f61e35d` then one squashed commit: `revert(activity): drop local tool-time derivation; server owns this`.\n\n- [ ] **Task R.2: Audit Chunk 1 outputs against new premise**\n\nRead each of: `focus_areas.go`, `badges.go`, `heatmap.go`, `metrics.go`. For each, decide keep / drop / defer. Expected outcomes:\n- `focus_areas.go` → drop (server labels replace the use case)\n- `badges.go` → defer (revisit during wireframing — see Task 6)\n- `heatmap.go` → keep (Week tab uses it)\n- `metrics.go` → keep, may reshape\n\nCommit removals as `refactor(activity): drop focus-area rule engine (superseded by server labels)`.\n\n- [ ] **Task R.3: Archive old plan**\n\nRename `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-15-entire-activity.md` to `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-15-entire-activity-v1-local-derivation.md`. Add one-line header: `> Superseded by 2026-04-21-entire-activity.md — premise shifted from local derivation to server aggregation.`\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 2: Aggregation primitives\n\nPure functions over projections. No I/O. Easy to TDD. @superpowers:test-driven-development\n\n### Task 1: `AggregateToolProfiles`\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/aggregate.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/aggregate_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```go\nfunc TestAggregateToolProfiles_SumsCounts(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    cps := []ActivityCheckpoint{\n        {ToolProfile: &ToolProfile{Total: 10, Categories: map[string]ToolCategoryMetrics{\"shell\": {Count: 7}, \"fileOps\": {Count: 3}}}},\n        {ToolProfile: &ToolProfile{Total: 4, Categories: map[string]ToolCategoryMetrics{\"shell\": {Count: 1}, \"search\": {Count: 3}}}},\n    }\n    got := AggregateToolProfiles(cps)\n    if got.Total != 14 { t.Fatalf(\"total=%d want 14\", got.Total) }\n    if got.Categories[\"shell\"].Count != 8 { t.Errorf(\"shell=%d want 8\", got.Categories[\"shell\"].Count) }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Verify test fails** (`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/activity/ -run AggregateToolProfiles`)\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**\n\n```go\nfunc AggregateToolProfiles(cps []ActivityCheckpoint) *ToolProfile {\n    out := &ToolProfile{Categories: map[string]ToolCategoryMetrics{}}\n    for _, c := range cps {\n        if c.ToolProfile == nil { continue }\n        out.Total += c.ToolProfile.Total\n        for k, v := range c.ToolProfile.Categories {\n            m := out.Categories[k]\n            m.Count += v.Count\n            out.Categories[k] = m\n        }\n    }\n    if out.Total == 0 { return nil }\n    return out\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Cases:** nil ToolProfile entries, empty input, all-nil result. Add tests for each.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** `feat(activity): aggregate tool profiles across checkpoints`\n\n### Task 2: `AggregateLabels`\n\nSame file. Sum counts per label across a checkpoint slice; return sorted-by-count slice of `{Label, Count}` pairs.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Failing test** (two checkpoints with overlapping labels; assert sorted-desc output).\n- [ ] **Step 2-4: Implement + test + commit** as `feat(activity): aggregate labels across checkpoints`.\n\n### Task 3: `AggregateAgents`\n\nReturns `[]AgentAggregation{AgentType, SessionCount, CheckpointCount, Tokens, TopLabels[:3], TopSkills[:3], TopMCPServers[:3]}`.\n\n- [ ] **Steps 1-4:** Define `AgentAggregation` type in `model.go`, write failing test with 2 agents × 2 checkpoints each, implement as single pass over `ActivitySession` list grouped by `AgentType`, commit.\n\n### Task 4: `FilterByRange`\n\n```go\nfunc FilterByRange(sessions []ActivitySession, start, end time.Time) []ActivitySession\n```\n\nFilters sessions whose `StartedAt` or `LastInteractionTime` falls within `[start, end]`. Half-open `[start, end)` to avoid double-counting midnight boundaries.\n\n- [ ] **Steps 1-4:** TDD, including edge cases (session spanning boundary, start == end, zero-value time).\n\n### Task 5: Range helpers\n\n**Files:** Append to `aggregate.go`.\n\nPure helpers that take `now time.Time` and return `(start, end)`:\n- `RangeToday(now)`, `RangeLastWeek(now)`, `RangeLastMonth(now)`, `RangeLast30d(now)`, `RangeLast90d(now)`\n\n- [ ] **Steps 1-4:** TDD with a fixed `now` fixture; cover DST edge behavior (just document the choice — we use local-time midnight boundaries).\n\n### Chunk 2 review checkpoint\n\n- [ ] Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test`.\n- [ ] All new tests green, no new lint findings.\n- [ ] @superpowers:verification-before-completion\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 3: Wireframes + static rendering\n\n### Task 6: Wireframe the three tabs\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `docs/2026-04-21-entire-activity-wireframes.md`\n\n**No code.** Draw each tab as ASCII-art mockups showing: column layout, color/weight accents (in prose), toggle position on Agents, empty-state text, and badge positions **if badges survive wireframing**. Explicitly decide each badge: keep / drop.\n\nThis task gates Task 7-9. Do not implement rendering until wireframes are approved.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Draw Day tab mockup.**\n- [ ] **Step 2: Draw Week tab mockup** (strip on top, list on bottom).\n- [ ] **Step 3: Draw Agents tab mockup** (toggle state + per-agent rows).\n- [ ] **Step 4: Decide badges** — write a one-line decision per candidate badge (`● active`, `▶ resumed`, etc.) under a \"Badges\" section.\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** `docs(activity): v2 wireframes for day/week/agents tabs`.\n\n### Task 7: Static renderer for Day tab\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/render_day.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/render_day_test.go`\n\nPure function `RenderDay(data DayView, opts RenderOpts) string`. Golden-file test against fixed fixtures. Uses existing `lipgloss` palette.\n\n- [ ] **Steps 1-5:** Fixture → failing golden test → implement → pass → commit.\n\n### Task 8: Static renderer for Week tab\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/render_week.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/render_week_test.go`\n\nReuses `heatmap.Bucketize` for the strip. Golden-file test.\n\n### Task 9: Static renderer for Agents tab\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/render_agents.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/render_agents_test.go`\n\nTakes a `RangeKey` enum (`day|week|month|30d|90d`). Golden-file test per range.\n\n### Chunk 3 review checkpoint\n\n- [ ] Wireframes reviewed (visual sanity — does the layout breathe?).\n- [ ] Static output golden-tested.\n- [ ] Accessible mode (`ACCESSIBLE=1`) produces plain-text equivalents.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 4: Command wiring + TUI\n\n### Task 10: Cobra command + subcommands\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/commands/activity.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/commands/activity_test.go`\n\n`entire activity` → opens TUI on Day. Subcommands `entire activity day|week|agents` open their tab directly. `--range day|week|month|30d|90d` on the agents subcommand only.\n\n- [ ] **Steps 1-5:** Failing test (subcommand dispatch) → implement with cobra → pass → commit.\n\n### Task 11: Bubbletea TUI skeleton\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/activity/tui.go`\n\nThree-tab state machine. `1/2/3` jump to tab; `tab` / `shift-tab` cycle; `q` quits. Agents tab reads toggle state from model.\n\n- [ ] Minimal model + update + view. Static renderers supply the panels.\n\n### Task 12: Range toggle on Agents tab\n\nLocal state: current `RangeKey`. Keys `d/w/m/3/9` cycle the toggle (or arrow keys). Re-aggregates on change.\n\n### Task 13: Integration test\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/activity_test.go`\n\nBuild tag `integration`. Seed a `testutil` repo with fake sessions + checkpoints, run `entire activity day`, assert static output matches golden.\n\n### Chunk 4 review checkpoint\n\n- [ ] `mise run check` green.\n- [ ] Manual smoke: run `entire activity` in this repo and look at the three tabs. If real data lands incoherently, iterate.\n- [ ] @superpowers:requesting-code-review before merge.\n\n---\n\n## Future / optional\n\n**Export.** Add `entire activity report --template daily|weekly --format markdown|json`. Reuses the renderers' underlying view structs via a JSON-marshal path; markdown is a second template set. Deferred until v1 proves useful.\n\n**History tab.** If weekly view proves too short-horizon, add `entire activity history` spanning multiple months. Only worth building once we have range-toggle feedback.\n\n**Repos tab.** Would aggregate by repo rather than agent. Only useful if users work across many repos from one shell. Defer.\n"},"cal