{"parentUuid":"cefca365-a2d2-4221-b68d-d3f3015ebff5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01H7TGLEwHkwtZwyZApUHjs9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BCLkth9JQSzHv8FkmxL3Pq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-21-entire-recap.md","content":"# Entire Recap Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Ship `entire recap`: a terminal view over existing server checkpoint analyses + local session state, surfacing what happened, when, and what the user should do next.\n\n**Architecture:** The CLI does not derive new metrics. It retrieves data that already exists (server `CheckpointAnalysis`, local `session.State`, `Entire-Checkpoint` commit trailers), aggregates it for a time range, runs a handful of insight primitives, and renders it in the terminal with a 4-panel layout. All computation is grouping + summing + single-pass reductions — no transcript walking, no local classification.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, `cobra` (command), `bubbletea` + `lipgloss` (TUI), existing `activity` package (projections, loaders, heatmap, metrics), existing `api` client (enrichment).\n\n**Naming note:** This supersedes our in-progress \"entire activity\" draft — `entire activity` is owned by PR #999 (different stats/metrics surface). Our work ships as `entire recap` to avoid collision.\n\n**Supersedes plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-15-entire-activity-v1-local-derivation.md` — original premise assumed local tool-time derivation. Server-side checkpoint analysis is now the authoritative source.\n\n---\n\n## Premise and data sources\n\n**What the CLI aggregates (already produced elsewhere):**\n\n| Source | Data |\n|---|---|\n| Server `CheckpointAnalysis` | labels, toolProfile, skillsUsed, mcpServersUsed, agentsUsed, modelsUsed, token totals |\n| Local `session.State` | agent, timestamps, files touched, checkpoints, session-level token usage |\n| Git (`Entire-Checkpoint` trailer) | checkpoint → commit linkage |\n\n**Out of scope for v1:** local tool-time derivation, transcript walkers, focus-area rule engine, profile variants (personal/team/observability), history/repos/report tabs.\n\n**Optional / future:** `--format json` / `--format markdown` export — noted as an explicit follow-up below.\n\n---\n\n## Command surface\n\n```\nentire recap [RANGE] [--agent <name>] [--format tui|static|json|markdown]\n\nRANGE (pick one — default: --day):\n  --day          today\n  --week         last 7 days\n  --month        this calendar month\n  --30           rolling 30 days\n  --90           rolling 90 days\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```\nentire recap                              # TUI, today, all agents\nentire recap --week                       # TUI, last 7 days, all agents\nentire recap --30 --agent claude-code     # TUI, 30 days, Claude Code only\nentire recap --week --format markdown     # non-interactive markdown output\nentire recap --day | head                 # piped → static mode\n```\n\n**TUI keyboard shortcuts:**\n\n- `1 2 3 4 5` or `d w m 3 9` — cycle range\n- `a` — cycle agent filter (all → claude-code → codex → gemini → …)\n- `enter` — drill into selected session row\n- `q` — quit\n\n---\n\n## View layout\n\nOne consistent 4-panel layout. Chronological session list (flat, not grouped). Panels:\n\n1. **Summary band** — top agent · dominant label · top skill · top model, plus totals\n2. **Activity strip** — range-appropriate heatmap (24h for `--day`, 7 cells for `--week`, day cells for `--30/--90`, calendar-aligned for `--month`)\n3. **Session list** — chronological, per-row badge + agent + span + labels + checkpoints + action hint\n4. **Worktrees │ Label distribution** — 2-column bottom panel\n\n### Mockup (Day range, ~100-column terminal)\n\n```\n  ╭─ Today ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n  │                                                                      │\n  │   Top agent     claude-code          Top skill     superpowers        │\n  │   Dominant     ▪ bug_fix  62%        Top model     opus-4-7           │\n  │                                                                      │\n  │   Totals       12 sessions · 47 checkpoints · 142k tokens · 8 commits │\n  │                                                                      │\n  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n  Activity (24h)\n  ░░▒▒▓▓██▓▓▒▒░░░░░░░░░░░░▒▒▓▓▓▓░░░░░░░\n  00  03  06  09  12  15  18  21\n\n  ╭─ Sessions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n  │                                                                      │\n  │   ● claude-code   2h   ▪ bug_fix          4 cp   ▶ resume            │\n  │   ● codex         1h   ▪ feature_build    2 cp   ⇈ commit            │\n  │   ◌ gemini       30m   ▪ refactor         1 cp   ↑ push              │\n  │   ◌ claude-code   4h   ▪ testing          6 cp   ⌫ clean             │\n  │                                                                      │\n  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n  Worktrees                          Labels\n  964-all-agents    3 sess  ⇈        bug_fix        ▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰  45%\n  entire-activity   2 sess           feature_build  ▰▰▰▰▰     28%\n  entire-attach     1 sess           refactor       ▰▰▰       15%\n\n  d w m 3 9  range  ·  a  agent filter  ·  ↵  details  ·  q  quit\n```\n\n### Mockup (Week range)\n\nSame four panels; **Activity strip** becomes a 7-cell heatmap ramp; summary band shows WoW delta arrows; session list collapses multi-day by day header with rows underneath.\n\n---\n\n## Visual language (matches PR #999 + existing CLI conventions)\n\nReuse palette already established in `search_tui.go`, `status_style.go`, and PR #999's `activity_render.go`:\n\n| Role | lipgloss color | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| primary accent | `\"214\"` amber | panel titles, active tab, agent names, commit markers |\n| muted | `\"8\"` dark gray | labels, units, placeholder text |\n| help hints | `\"241\"` / `\"245\"` | keybind hints at footer |\n| separators | `\"240\"` / `\"243\"` | panel borders, divider lines |\n| success / add | `\"2\"` green | `↑ push`, additions, green badge |\n| error / delete | `\"1\"` red | destructive hints, deletions |\n| warn | `\"3\"` yellow | `⌫ clean` hint, stale markers |\n| info | `\"6\"` cyan | `▶ resume` hint |\n| neutral | `\"7\"` light gray | default body text |\n\n**Style struct pattern:** define styles by semantic role, not by literal color. Follow PR #999's `activityStyles` shape:\n\n```go\ntype recapStyles struct {\n    bold, dim, label, value, unit      lipgloss.Style\n    title, accent                      lipgloss.Style  // 214 amber\n    border                             lipgloss.Style  // 243\n    add, del, warn, info, muted        lipgloss.Style  // 2,1,3,6,8\n    hintResume, hintCommit,\n    hintPush, hintClean                lipgloss.Style\n}\nfunc newRecapStyles(useColor bool) recapStyles { … }\n```\n\n**Spacing discipline** (this was the \"spec looks tight\" fix):\n\n- One blank line above and below each panel\n- Panel content has 2 spaces of left/right padding inside the border\n- Table columns separated by ≥3 spaces, or a `·` bullet when inline\n- Footer help line sits on its own line with 1 blank line of clearance above\n- Prefer panel width up to terminal width (use `lipgloss.Width` to measure), with a sensible minimum (~80 cols) and graceful degradation narrower\n\n**TTY detection:** `shouldUseColor(w io.Writer) bool` — matches PR #999's helper. When piped or `ACCESSIBLE=1`, render plain text with ASCII fallbacks (`•` instead of `●`, `>` instead of `▶`, no borders