{"parentUuid":"7c687129-a886-4ec0-a4a4-10b203194e0b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-21-entire-recap.md","snippet":"1\t# Entire Recap Implementation Plan\n2\t\n3\t> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n4\t\n5\t**Goal:** Ship `entire recap`: a terminal view over existing server checkpoint analyses + local session state, surfacing what happened, when, and what the user should do next.\n6\t\n7\t**Architecture:** The CLI does not derive new metrics. It retrieves data that already exists (server `CheckpointAnalysis`, local `session.State`, `Entire-Checkpoint` commit trailers), aggregates it for a time range, runs a handful of insight primitives, and renders it in the terminal with a 4-panel layout. All computation is grouping + summing + single-pass reductions — no transcript walking, no local classification.\n8\t\n9\t**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, `cobra` (command), `bubbletea` + `lipgloss` (TUI), existing `activity` package (projections, loaders, heatmap, metrics), existing `api` client (enrichment).\n10\t\n11\t**Naming note:** This supersedes our in-progress \"entire activity\" draft — `entire activity` is owned by PR #999 (different stats/metrics surface). Our work ships as `entire recap` to avoid collision.\n12\t\n13\t**Supersedes plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-15-entire-activity-v1-local-derivation.md` — original premise assumed local tool-time derivation. Server-side checkpoint analysis is now the authoritative source.\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## Premise and data sources\n18\t\n19\t**What the CLI aggregates (already produced elsewhere):**\n20\t\n21\t| Data surface | Source | Concrete location |\n22\t|---|---|---|\n23\t| Session (agent, timestamps, files, phase, tokens) | Local | `.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json` |\n24\t| Checkpoint evidence tree | Local | `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch, sharded `<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/` |\n25\t| Commit ↔ checkpoint linkage | Local | git log + `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer |\n26\t| Labels, toolProfile, skillsUsed, mcpServersUsed, agentsUsed, modelsUsed, totalTokens | Server (per checkpoint) | `GET /:org/:repo/checkpoints/:id/analysis` (entire.io `cache.ts:4585`) |\n27\t| Repo identity (org/name) | Derived | `parseGitRemoteURL(git remote get-url origin)` — reuse `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go` |\n28\t\n29\t**Note:** `enrich.go:70-73` has a stale comment claiming the enrichment endpoint path is \"an assumption.\" It isn't — update that comment during Chunk R cleanup.\n30\t\n31\t**Out of scope for v1:** local tool-time derivation, transcript walkers, focus-area rule engine, profile variants (personal/team/observability), history/repos/report tabs.\n32\t\n33\t**Optional / future:** `--format json` / `--format markdown` export — noted as an explicit follow-up below.\n34\t\n35\t---\n36\t\n37\t## Command surface\n38\t\n39\t```\n40\tentire recap [RANGE] [--agent <name>] [--format tui|static|json|markdown]\n41\t\n42\tRANGE (pick one — default: --day):\n43\t  --day          today\n44\t  --week         last 7 days\n45\t  --month        this calendar month\n46\t  --30           rolling 30 days\n47\t  --90           rolling 90 days\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\t**Examples:**\n51\t\n52\t```\n53\tentire recap                              # TUI, today, all agents\n54\tentire recap --week                       # TUI, last 7 days, all agents\n55\tentire recap --30 --agent claude-code     # TUI, 30 days, Claude Code only\n56\tentire recap --week --format markdown     # non-interactive markdown output\n57\tentire recap --day | head                 # piped → static mode\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t**TUI keyboard shortcuts:**\n61\t\n62\t- `1 2 3 4 5` or `d w m 3 9` — cycle range\n63\t- `a` — cycle agent filter (all → claude-code → codex → gemini → …)\n64\t- `enter` — drill into selected session row\n65\t- `q` — quit\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## View layout\n70\t\n71\tOne consistent 4-panel layout. Chronological session list (flat, not grouped). Panels:\n72\t\n73\t1. **Summary band** — top agent · dominant label · top skill · top model, plus totals\n74\t2. **Activity strip** — range-appropriate heatmap (24h for `--day`, 7 cells for `--week`, day cells for `--30/--90`, calendar-aligned for `--month`)\n75\t3. **Session list** — chronological, per-row badge + agent + repo (slug) + span + labels + checkpoints + action hint\n76\t4. **Repos · Worktrees · Labels** — 3-column bottom panel:\n77\t   - **Repos** — distinct `org/repo` slugs across the range (hidden when all sessions share one repo — keeps Day view uncluttered for single-repo users)\n78\t   - **Worktrees** — within-repo parallel streams\n79\t   - **Labels** — gradient-bar distribution\n80\t\n81\t### Mockup (Day range, ~100-column terminal)\n82\t\n83\t```\n84\t  ╭─ Today ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n85\t  │                                                                      │\n86\t  │   Top agent     claude-code          Top skill     superpowers        │\n87\t  │   Dominant     ▪ bug_fix  62%        Top model     opus-4-7           │\n88\t  │                                                                      │\n89\t  │   Totals       12 sessions · 47 checkpoints · 142k tokens · 8 commits │\n90\t  │                                                                      │\n91\t  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n92\t\n93\t  Activity (24h)\n94\t  ░░▒▒▓▓██▓▓▒▒░░░░░░░░░░░░▒▒▓▓▓▓░░░░░░░\n95\t  00  03  06  09  12  15  18  21\n96\t\n97\t  ╭─ Sessions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n98\t  │                                                                      │\n99\t  │   ● claude-code   2h   ▪ bug_fix          4 cp   ▶ resume            │\n100\t  │   ● codex         1h   ▪ feature_build    2 cp   ⇈ commit            │\n101\t  │   ◌ gemini       30m   ▪ refactor         1 cp   ↑ push              │\n102\t  │   ◌ claude-code   4h   ▪ testing          6 cp   ⌫ clean             │\n103\t  │                                                                      │\n104\t  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n105\t\n106\t  Repos                   Worktrees                    Labels\n107\t  entireio/cli    5 sess  964-all-agents   3 sess  ⇈   bug_fix        ▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰  45%\n108\t  entireio/ent.io 1 sess  entire-activity  2 sess      feature_build  ▰▰▰▰▰     28%\n109\t                          entire-attach    1 sess      refactor       ▰▰▰       15%\n110\t\n111\t  d w m 3 9  range  ·  a  agent filter  ·  ↵  details  ·  q  quit\n112\t```\n113\t\n114\t### Mockup (Week range)\n115\t\n116\tSame four panels; **Activity strip** becomes a 7-cell heatmap ramp; summary band shows WoW delta arrows; session list collapses multi-day by day header with rows underneath.\n117\t\n118\t---\n119\t\n120\t## Visual language (matches PR #999 + existing CLI conventions)\n121\t\n122\tReuse palette already established in `search_tui.go`, `status_style.go`, and PR #999's `activity_render.go`:\n123\t\n124\t| Role | lipgloss color | Use |\n125\t|---|---|---|\n126\t| primary accent | `\"214\"` amber | panel titles, active tab, agent names, commit markers |\n127\t| muted | `\"8\"` dark gray | labels, units, placeholder text |\n128\t| help hints | `\"241\"` / `\"245\"` | keybind hints at footer |\n129\t| separators | `\"240\"` / `\"243\"` | panel borders, divider lines |\n130\t| success / add | `\"2\"` green | `↑ push`, additions, green badge |\n131\t| error / delete | `\"1\"` red | destructive hints, deletions |\n132\t| warn | `\"3\"` yellow | `⌫ clean` hint, stale markers |\n133\t| info | `\"6\"` cyan | `▶ resume` hint |\n134\t| neutral | `\"7\"` light gray | default body text |\n135\t\n136\t**Style struct pattern:** define styles by semantic role, not by literal color. Follow PR #999's `activityStyles` shape:\n137\t\n138\t```go\n139\ttype recapStyles struct {\n140\t    bold, dim, label, value, unit      lipgloss.Style\n141\t    title, accent                      lipgloss.Style  // 214 amber\n142\t    border                             lipgloss.Style  // 243\n143\t    add, del, warn, info, muted        lipgloss.Style  // 2,1,3,6,8\n144\t    hintResume, hintCommit,\n145\t    hintPush, hintClean                lipgloss.Style\n146\t}\n147\tfunc newRecapStyles(useColor bool) recapStyles { … }\n148\t```\n149\t\n150\t**Spacing discipline** (this was the \"spec looks tight\" fix):\n151\t\n152\t- One blank line above and below each panel\n\n... [260 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ace23b01-0df7-4f15-afdb-c28223b8a58a","timestamp":"2026-04-21T23:15:26.309Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity"}
