{"parentUuid":"5c7e11f3-debe-48dc-b16e-63c14725b475","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SUie3FsPBEuMqxFbDjLMSz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's how it would look integrated. Rough mockup first, then the toggle.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Side-by-side \"me vs team\" makes the comparison obvious at a glance — the number on the left is yours, the number on the right is everyone else. Context-switching overhead is near-zero. That's what the user actually wants from a team dashboard.\n- A toggle to cycle between **me / team / both** lets scanners pick their focus. `both` is the default (richest info); `me` for solo work review; `team` when you want to see what patterns to adopt.\n- Team data piggybacks on the same per-agent card layout. No second visual language — same mini-bars, same chips, just a second column. Low rendering cost for the second dimension.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Agents tab — combined layout (default: me + team)\n\n```\n╭─ Agents · Week · me + team ────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│  Range: day  [week]  month  30d  90d      View: me  team  [both]  │\n╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n╭─ claude-code ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                             me              team                    │\n│   Sessions                  12              89                      │\n│   Tokens                  142k            1.2M                      │\n│   Checkpoints               47             312                      │\n│                                                                     │\n│   Top labels (bars)                                                 │\n│     bug_fix     ▰▰▰▰▰▰ 45%      feature_build ▰▰▰▰▰ 38%            │\n│     feature     ▰▰▰▰   28%      bug_fix       ▰▰▰▰  32%            │\n│     refactor    ▰▰     15%      testing       ▰▰    18%            │\n│                                                                     │\n│   Top skills    superpowers, brainstorming     superpowers, writing │\n│   Top models    opus-4-7, sonnet-4-6           opus-4-7, sonnet-4-6 │\n│   Top repos     entireio/cli (5), ent.io (3)   entireio/cli (62)    │\n╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n╭─ codex ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│   Sessions       3      11                                          │\n│   Tokens        45k    180k                                         │\n│   Top labels    refactor 60%     refactor 48%                       │\n│   Top repos     entireio/cli (3) entireio/cli (11)                  │\n╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n  1 2 3 4 5  range  ·  v  view (me/team/both)  ·  a  agent filter  ·  q  quit\n```\n\n## Toggle semantics\n\n- `v` cycles `both → me → team → both`\n- `both` is default → maximum info density\n- `me` → collapses right column, widens left for drill-down details (what skills I used most, which commits, etc.)\n- `team` → collapses left, shows who else on the team and their highlights\n- `--view <me|team|both>` flag for static mode\n\n## Data wiring (no new server work)\n\n| Column | Source | Endpoint |\n|---|---|---|\n| **me** | local session state + per-checkpoint analysis I already fetch | `GET /:org/:repo/checkpoints/:id/analysis` |\n| **team** | server's existing repo-overview endpoints | `agent-activity`, `contributor-agents`, `contributor-tokens`, `session-patterns` |\n\nThe team endpoints are already authed and deployed. CLI just needs to fetch them when logged in and a repo is identified.\n\n## Scope for one commit\n\n1. `AgentsCard` rendering (the per-agent panel composing me + team columns)\n2. Team data client: `recap/team.go` — single file, fetches the 3-4 overview endpoints, combines into per-agent team summary\n3. Agents view becomes the default layout in `View`; current chronological layout accessible via `v` toggle in TUI or `--view sessions` flag\n4. Default range becomes **week** (not today) — matches the \"what's my team up to\" question better\n5. Tests: card rendering, team fetch mocked, toggle state transitions\n\n**What's deferred:** solo-user graceful fallback (show \"no team data\" when repo isn't tracked), weighted comparisons (\"you're ahead of team in X\"), and historical me-vs-team trend lines. All future polish.\n\n## Questions before I build\n\n1. **`both` layout**: side-by-side columns like I mocked, or stacked (me section, then team section below, no columns)? Columns make direct comparison easier; stacking reads more like prose.\n2. **When team data is unavailable** (solo user, repo not tracked, not logged in): fall back to me-only layout silently, or show \"team data requires login / repo tracking\" placeholder?\n\nAnswer those two and I'll build it. Otherwise I'll default to **columns** + **silent fallback** since those are the simpler UX."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2660,"cache_read_input_tokens":533746,"output_tokens":3476,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2660},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3476,"cache_read_input_tokens":533746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2660,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaHs5UjdTaVfHztkVRfRM","type":"assistant","uuid":"978921b9-22a7-41f5-a0b5-e138f30420ae","timestamp":"2026-04-22T00:30:09.063Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf",