{"parentUuid":"da409530-c82f-4136-8aeb-8224f312fbf9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SceCzuH5VxYcwbfGZLgKp1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Checked the entire.io model. Here's what \"team\" actually means in the system.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- There is no explicit \"team\" or \"organization\" table. Authorization is **per-user-per-repo** via the `user_repos` join table. `checkRepoAccess` returns a single `RepoRecord`, not a team.\n- The overview endpoints use **\"contributor\"** (matching GitHub's language), not \"team\". `contributor-tokens`, `contributor-agents`, `agent-activity` aggregate across everyone who has committed to the repo. So \"team\" in our CLI really means \"everyone contributing to this repo.\"\n- Scope is **per-repo**. If you work across multiple repos, each repo has its own contributor set. There's no server-side notion of \"my teammates across all my repos.\"\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## What this means for scoping\n\n**Team = repo contributors, per-repo.** No ambiguity, no user-management flow needed — the server already knows who contributed because GitHub auth established access via `user_repos`. Solo repos naturally have a team of 1 (just you). Multi-contributor repos have real comparison data.\n\n**No \"add users\" step needed.** The contributor set is derived from:\n1. GitHub authentication + repo access (who's logged in)\n2. Commit authorship (whose commits have `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers)\n\nYou already don't need to curate this list — entire.io does it automatically from the commits it sees.\n\n**Naming recommendation:** call it **\"team\"** in the UI (friendly, short), but be accurate about scope in the help text: *\"Everyone contributing to this repo.\"*\n\n## Revised scoping for the Agents view\n\n**When the team panel shows data:**\n- Logged in (auth token present) ✓\n- Current repo is tracked in entire.io (has a `RepoRecord`) ✓\n- Repo has >1 contributor (otherwise the team column == you, which is noise)\n\n**When it doesn't:**\n- Not logged in → \"Sign in with `entire login` to see team data\"\n- Repo not tracked → \"This repo isn't tracked in entire.io yet\"\n- Solo repo (only one contributor) → just hide the team column for this repo\n\n**Multi-repo behavior:** if your current sessions span multiple repos, the team column aggregates across each repo's contributor data — but the card notes the per-repo breakdown (e.g., \"claude-code · team: 89 sess across 2 repos\").\n\n## Scope for the colorful v1\n\nOne commit. Will build:\n1. **`recap/team.go`** — fetches `agent-activity`, `contributor-agents`, `contributor-tokens` for the current repo(s) over the range, merges into a per-agent team summary\n2. **`AgentsCard` renderer** — lipgloss-heavy: amber accent on agent names, green on token totals, cyan on skill chips, label bars in their canonical colors. Side-by-side me/team columns, nicely padded\n3. **View toggle** — `v` cycles me/team/both (default both)\n4. **Range default** — week\n5. **Graceful fallbacks** — silent hide of team column when solo/not-tracked; non-blocking \"sign in to see team\" hint at bottom when unauthed\n6. **Tests** — fixture-based for cards + fallback paths\n\nSound good? One confirmation and I'll build."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1743,"cache_read_input_tokens":541676,"output_tokens":2009,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1743},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2009,"cache_read_input_tokens":541676,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1743,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_0