{"parentUuid":"6d70be7d-8ab1-462e-b7e0-d2f9c7309e56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XDsEU6QSNVD4sNah3crFYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agents view landed. Commit `c243ded3c`.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The `—` em-dash (vs `-`) is a deliberate choice in the contributors column placeholder: it reads as \"intentionally absent\" rather than \"this number is zero.\" When server data lands in a follow-up, the em-dashes fill in with real numbers.\n- Defaulting the range to `--week` matches what Agents view is actually good at: single-day Agents data is usually too sparse (one agent, a handful of checkpoints), while a week's worth gives enough for real comparisons. Day-level detail is still reachable via `--day`.\n- The `ContribCount` field (distinct contributors) is the coolest contributor-column field for a solo dev: it shows you're working alone (1) vs on a team (5). Gives users a clear signal about whether the team column is worth paying attention to.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## What's callable now\n\n```\nentire recap                              # Agents view, week, me+contributors, TUI\nentire recap --day                        # today only\nentire recap --30 --agent claude-code     # 30d, one agent\nentire recap --view me                    # hide contributors column\nentire recap --view contributors          # just the repo-wide aggregate\nentire recap --week | head                # piped → static Agents layout\n```\n\nIn TUI: `v` cycles me/contributors/both; `a` cycles agents; `1-5` or `d/w/m` changes range.\n\n## What's landing in the next commit (follow-up)\n\n- **Wire the contributor data.** One new file `recap/contributors.go` that:\n  1. Takes the current repo (via `ResolveRepoFromWorktree`)\n  2. Calls `/:org/:repo/overview/agent-activity`, `/contributor-tokens`, `/contributor-agents`\n  3. Merges responses into `ContribSessions` / `ContribTokens` / `ContribCount` / `ContribLabels` per agent card\n\nThe Chunk 5b commit's placeholder em-dashes fill in with real numbers the moment that's done.\n\n## Smoke test?\n\nWant me to try running `entire recap` in this repo to see what it looks like with your real session data? That'll catch any rendering bugs the unit tests missed and give you a visual confirmation the palette works before we wire up contributors."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":586664,"output_tokens":1034,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1034,"cache_read_input_tokens":586664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaHtGgjccDEkFWBMoeJ2Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"298cc3e6-9a0e-4b7e-8ef7-1640ecf95d20","timestamp":"2026-04-22T00:45:17.224Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity"}
