{"parentUuid":"4bf02529-01ba-43a8-8f43-48e9f582ca3c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013w14h72Fs2a49TrMdCHBEC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Different fields come from different parts of the pipeline — so \"no summaries\" doesn't mean \"no data.\"\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- `StoredCheckpointAnalysis` is assembled at `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts:648` from TWO sources: `generateCheckpointAnalysis` (the **LLM** call, produces `extraction.labels` and `extraction.summary`) and `extractToolMetrics` (**deterministic** transcript parsing, produces `skillsUsed`, `mcpServersUsed`, `toolProfile`). Plus `extractModelsUsedFromSessionMetadata` for `modelsUsed`.\n- If the LLM run is skipped or failed, `extraction` is absent (no labels, no summary) — but `skillsUsed`/`mcpServersUsed`/`toolProfile`/`modelsUsed` are STILL populated because they come from deterministic parsing that doesn't touch the LLM.\n- If the whole pipeline never ran (no `analysis_json` written), nothing exists and the endpoint returns `status: \"not_available\"` or `\"pending\"`.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## What survives without summaries\n\n| Field | Source | Survives \"no summaries\"? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `extraction.labels` | LLM (generateCheckpointAnalysis) | ❌ — tied to summary generation |\n| `extraction.summary` | LLM | ❌ — the thing that's missing |\n| `skillsUsed` | deterministic parse of transcript | ✅ |\n| `mcpServersUsed` | deterministic parse | ✅ |\n| `toolProfile` | deterministic parse | ✅ |\n| `modelsUsed` | session metadata | ✅ |\n| `agentsUsed` | session metadata | ✅ |\n| `total_transcript_tokens` | metadata sum | ✅ |\n| `totalFilesChanged` | commit stats | ✅ |\n\n## What this means for `entire recap`\n\n- **If LLM is on, everything works** — both columns get labels, skills, mcp, tool-mix.\n- **If LLM is off / rate-limited**, labels go empty on both me + contributor sides. Skills / MCP / tool-mix / tokens / counts all still populate. So the \"Top skills\", \"MCP servers\", \"Tool mix\" rows will have values; \"Top labels\" will show `—`.\n- **If analysis never ran**, nothing — status is `pending` / `not_available`, everything shows `—`.\n\nThe local-fallback idea maps onto this cleanly: tool-time + skills are deterministic, so CLI can derive them from transcripts without the server. Labels always need the server because they require LLM classification.\n\n**Recap-specific implication:** don't treat \"no labels\" as \"no data.\" Render the deterministic fields (tokens, skills, mcp, tool-mix, counts) even when labels are empty, and show a specific hint for the labels row rather than collapsing the whole card.\n\nWant me to:\n1. Finalize the server `/me/recap` draft to also return the deterministic fields when `extraction` is missing (it already does since I read `skillsUsed`/`mcpServersUsed`/`toolProfile` separately)?\n2. Add a per-row `—` with a tooltip-style reason on the labels row specifically when extraction is missing?\n3. Land the local fallback for tool-time + skills in the CLI (independent of server state)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2803,"cache_read_input_tokens":911208,"output_tokens":1836,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2803,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1836,"cache_read_input_tokens":911208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2803},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKgUnByW8AgDrhrgpZiR","type":"assistant","uuid":"53888c14-f5ba-47d8-b2c6-2af9a8749561","timestamp":"2026-04-22T23:31:59.764Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/p