{"parentUuid":"90e5a1d2-6a68-4722-a211-daae20317137","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"974197e9-f039-4ca6-bbf9-27797508d17b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeQt8pogGT6AsG1ge32FVY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Entire Activity Design\n2\t\n3\tDate: 2026-04-15 (revised 2026-04-16)\n4\t\n5\t## Summary\n6\t\n7\t`entire activity` is a new read-only product surface for understanding work captured by Entire over time.\n8\t\n9\tIt is centered on:\n10\t\n11\t- **sessions** as the primary unit of work\n12\t- **checkpoints** as the evidence trail inside a session\n13\t- **repo, time, and agent** as first-class grouping dimensions\n14\t\n15\tThis is not a sprint tool and should not use sprint language. It is an Entire-native activity layer over existing session, checkpoint, transcript, and commit-linkage data — rendered as a tabbed dashboard in the terminal.\n16\t\n17\t## Goals\n18\t\n19\t- Show what happened today and across selectable time ranges.\n20\t- Make checkpoint and session activity easy to scan quickly.\n21\t- Surface useful, defensible insights instead of generic churn metrics.\n22\t- Support today / range / history / agents / repos / report tabs in v1.\n23\t- Support interactive TUI and static output in v1.\n24\t- Use only metrics that are directly available now or safely derivable from existing data.\n25\t- Reuse existing CLI infrastructure (session state, checkpoint store, auth, lipgloss styles) rather than duplicating it.\n26\t\n27\t## Non-Goals\n28\t\n29\t- No productivity score.\n30\t- No “most modified files” leaderboard as a primary signal.\n31\t- No sprint framing.\n32\t- No LLM-generated prose in the CLI. (Server-side LLM classification is consumed as data, not re-generated locally.)\n33\t- No claims of labor time or focus time beyond actual timestamp spans.\n34\t- No local reimplementation of the server-side checkpoint analysis pipeline.\n35\t\n36\t## Product Definition\n37\t\n38\t`entire activity` answers:\n39\t\n40\t- what happened\n41\t- when it happened\n42\t- where it happened\n43\t- what kind of work it was\n44\t- which agents and models were involved\n45\t- which checkpoints linked to commits\n46\t- what should likely be resumed or finished\n47\t\n48\t## Information Architecture\n49\t\n50\tThe v1 surface is a **tabbed dashboard**. Six top-level tabs:\n51\t\n52\t```\n53\ttoday │ range │ history │ agents │ repos │ report\n54\t```\n55\t\n56\tRules:\n57\t\n58\t- Each tab is a self-contained view with its own panel layout. Panels never span tabs.\n59\t- Active tab is visually distinct (amber `214` with an underline rule); inactive tabs are faint gray `244`.\n60\t- Keyboard: `1-6` jump directly to a tab. `tab` / `shift-tab` cycle. `q` quits.\n61\t- Within a tab, arrow keys move between panels/rows. `enter` opens drill-down. `esc` closes drill-down.\n62\t- CLI subcommands map 1:1 to tabs: `entire activity today` opens the today tab, `entire activity agents` opens agents tab, etc.\n63\t\n64\tProfiles only change defaults and emphasis (heatmap metric, whether token panels are prominent, etc.):\n65\t\n66\t- `personal` (default)\n67\t- `team`\n68\t- `observability`\n69\t\n70\t## Command Surface\n71\t\n72\t```bash\n73\tentire activity                                 # opens TUI on 'today' tab\n74\tentire activity today\n75\tentire activity range --last 7d\n76\tentire activity range --from 2026-04-01 --to 2026-04-15\n77\tentire activity history\n78\tentire activity agents\n79\tentire activity repos\n80\tentire activity report --template daily --format markdown\n81\t```\n82\t\n83\tShared flags:\n84\t\n85\t```bash\n86\t--repo current|owner/name|all|local\n87\t--profile personal|team|observability\n88\t--from YYYY-MM-DD\n89\t--to YYYY-MM-DD\n90\t--last 7d|14d|30d\n91\t--group-by repo|day|agent\n92\t--view cards|table\n93\t--json\n94\t--local-only    # never call the api; labels unavailable\n95\t--no-color      # also honors NO_COLOR env var\n96\t```\n97\t\n98\tNotes:\n99\t\n100\t- `entire activity` (no args) opens the TUI on the `today` tab.\n101\t- `--repo all` is the default for logged-in users and covers every repo the user has api access to. `--repo current` narrows to the current worktree's repo. `--repo local` forces offline / this-repo-only mode.\n102\t- All subcommands support static terminal output and JSON output.\n103\t- `--json` output always includes `\"schema_version\": \"v1\"` at the top level.\n104\t\n105\t## Execution Model\n106\t\n107\t### Local-first, api-enriched\n108\t\n109\t- **Local is the default data source.** `entire activity today` with no login returns a complete, honest view of the current repo's activity using only local data.\n110\t- **API enrichment is lazy.** When `entire login` has produced a token, the CLI fetches server-authoritative labels and tool-time data per checkpoint. Enrichment fills in asynchronously in the TUI and is batched before final print in static mode.\n111\t- **Offline / not-logged-in fallback** is silent. Tab chrome shows a single line: `labels: offline · tip: run 'entire login' for agent insights`.\n112\t- **Performance budget:**\n113\t  - `today`: < 1s local, < 2s with api enrichment\n114\t  - `range --last 7d`: < 3s local, < 6s with enrichment\n115\t  - `range --last 30d`: < 6s local, < 12s with enrichment\n116\t  - `history` (90d): < 10s local, < 30s with enrichment\n117\t- **Cache** at `.git/entire-activity-cache/<checkpoint-id>.json` for api responses. Invalidated when `StoredCheckpointAnalysis.pipeline_version` changes.\n118\t\n119\t### Three-tier Data Truth Table\n120\t\n121\tEvery metric is sourced from exactly one tier. The UI tags metrics with their tier via the tab chrome footer (e.g. `labels: server · span: local · linked commits: local`).\n122\t\n123\t#### Tier 1 — Local-authoritative\n124\t\n125\tReadable from `.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json` (session state) and `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch (committed metadata):\n126\t\n127\t- session ID, checkpoint ID\n128\t- session started / ended / last-interaction timestamps\n129\t- session phase, step count\n130\t- checkpoint timestamps\n131\t- files touched per session / per checkpoint\n132\t- base commit, worktree path, worktree ID\n133\t- agent type, model name (when state records it)\n134\t- token usage (when the agent or hook reports it)\n135\t- prompt text (scoped per checkpoint)\n136\t- attribution metadata (`InitialAttribution`)\n137\t- `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer presence on user commits (via local `git log`)\n138\t- hook-provided session metrics (`SessionMetrics.DurationMs/TurnCount/ContextTokens`) for agents that emit them (e.g., Cursor)\n139\t\n140\t#### Tier 2 — Local-derivable\n141\t\n142\tCheap computation from tier 1 with no api call:\n143\t\n144\t- **session span minutes** = `last_checkpoint_ts − first_checkpoint_ts` (honest first-to-last timestamp, replaces the FE `max(steps) × 2 / 60` estimate)\n145\t- checkpoints per session, checkpoint density, median checkpoint gap\n146\t- sessions/day, checkpoints/day\n147\t- active day count, streaks (same algorithm as FE `useUserDashboardData.ts`)\n148\t- heatmap cell intensity\n149\t- intra-day hour buckets\n150\t- resume-after-gap detection\n151\t- focus area assignment from `files_touched` via rule engine\n152\t- linked commit count, linked commit rate (via `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer lookup)\n153\t- commit-linked vs exploratory-only split\n154\t- badges (`resumed`, `linked commit`, `delegated`, `multi-repo`)\n155\t- active-session rollups (un-pushed work that only exists locally)\n156\t\n157\t#### Tier 3 — Server-authoritative\n158\t\n159\tRequires `entire login` and a network round trip. Fetched per committed checkpoint and cached:\n160\t\n161\t- **work-mode labels** — `CheckpointExtraction.labels[]` from `StoredCheckpointAnalysis` (18-value multi-label taxonomy, max 3 per checkpoint)\n162\t- **`toolProfile.categories[*].count`** — tool usage counts (shell / fileOps / search / mcp / agent / other)\n163\t- **`toolProfile.categories[*].durationMs`** — tool time per category (**pending upstream server change**, see Upstream Dependencies)\n164\t- `skillsUsed`, `mcpServersUsed`, `modelsUsed`, `agentsUsed`\n165\t- execution feedback: `thrashing`, `bugProfile`, `architectureChanges`\n166\t- cross-repo aggregation for `--repo all`\n167\t- session span canonicalization (**pending** — until then CLI uses tier 2)\n168\t\n169\t## Core Data Model\n170\t\n171\tActivity types are **read-only projections**, not new primitives. They are built in `load.go` from existing `session.State` + `checkpoint.CheckpointSummary` + `checkpoint.CommittedMetadata` (+ optional api `StoredCheckpointAnalysis`). They are never persisted. The existing `session` and `checkpoint` packages remain the canonical owners of underlying data.\n172\t\n173\t### ActivitySession\n174\t\n175\tProjected from `session.State` + per-session checkpoint rollups. Key fields:\n176\t\n177\t- repo, session ID, branch (when available), worktree ID, worktree path\n178\t- started at, ended at, last interaction at\n179\t- span minutes (tier 2: honest, first→last checkpoint)\n180\t- step count, task checkpoint count\n181\t- checkpoints: `[]ActivityCheckpoint`\n182\t- agents used, models used\n183\t- focus areas (tier 2, from `files_touched`)\n184\t- labels (tier 3, from api; empty when offline)\n185\t- badges (tier 2, deterministic local)\n186\t- token totals (tier 1 when available)\n187\t- linked commit SHAs (tier 2)\n188\t- is active, is resumable\n189\t- `source` (local | server | mixed)\n190\t\n191\t### ActivityCheckpoint\n192\t\n193\tProjected from `checkpoint.CheckpointSummary` + `checkpoint.CommittedMetadata` (+ optional api). Key fields:\n194\t\n195\t- repo, session ID, checkpoint ID\n196\t- timestamp\n197\t- is task checkpoint, tool use ID\n198\t- agent, model\n199\t- focus areas (tier 2)\n200\t- linked commit SHA (tier 2)\n201\t- token usage (tier 1 when available)\n202\t- turn ID\n203\t- labels (tier 3, from api; empty when offline)\n204\t- tool profile (tier 3, from api; empty when offline)\n205\t- badges (tier 2)\n206\t- source\n207\t\n208\t### ActivityDay\n209\t\n210\tPer-day rollup. Key fields: date, repos, sessions, checkpoints, task checkpoints, linked commits, token totals, label counts, focus area counts, resume count, tool-time totals (tier 3).\n211\t\n212\t### ActivityRangeSummary\n213\t\n214\tRange-level aggregates. Fields include: from, to, repos touched, sessions, checkpoints, task checkpoints, linked commits, active days, tokens, label counts (with confidence gating, see below), focus area counts, agent counts, model counts, repo summaries, top sessions, tool-time totals.\n215\t\n216\t### ActivityRepoSummary / ActivityAgentSummary\n217\t\n218\tRepo- and agent-scoped rollups used in `repos` and `agents` tabs.\n219\t\n220\t## Labels — Server-Authoritative\n221\t\n222\t### Why No Local Classifier\n223\t\n224\tThe entire.io api already runs `checkpoint-analysis-pipeline.ts` (pipeline version `2026-04-10.v3`) which uses the Anthropic SDK to produce `CheckpointExtraction { labels[], blocks[] }`. Results are stored as `StoredCheckpointAnalysis` in the db. This is the same pipeline that drives the web app's checkpoint summary UI (PR #1021).\n225\t\n226\tA second classifier in the CLI would produce a different taxonomy, different weights, and eventual drift. Users would see `build` in the TUI and `feature_build` in the web app for the same checkpoint — a reportable bug. We avoid that by letting the server own classification and having the CLI consume and render.\n227\t\n228\t### Canonical Taxonomy\n229\t\n230\tLabels are multi-label with max 3 per checkpoint, drawn from `CHECKPOINT_LABELS` in `api/src/types.ts`:\n231\t\n232\t```\n233\tfeature_build, bug_fix, refactor, performance, optimization,\n234\tinvestigation, configuration, testing, deployment, recovery,\n235\tplanning, security_fix, documentation, migration, telemetry,\n236\tobservability, enhancement, dependencies\n237\t```\n238\t\n239\t### Rendering\n240\t\n241\t- Session cards and checkpoint rows show up to 3 label pills (semantic color per label; see Visual Language).\n242\t- Sessions without a server analysis render **unlabeled**, not as `mixed`. Offline mode suppresses label pills entirely and notes it in the chrome footer.\n243\t- Range-level \"modes\" panels aggregate by summing label occurrences across checkpoints/sessions.\n244\t- A range never claims a dominant mode unless: top label share ≥ 0.55 and top leads runner-up by ≥ 0.15. Otherwise render `Modes: feature_build 4 · bug_fix 3 · testing 2`.\n245\t\n246\t## Badges — Local Deterministic\n247\t\n248\tBadges are cheap local facts, not classifications. They don't require the api.\n249\t\n250\t- `⚑ linked` — session has at least one `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer on an active-branch commit\n251\t- `↻ resumed` — session started after ≥ 6h gap from the prior session on the same branch\n252\t- `⇢ delegated` — session has task checkpoint count ≥ 1\n253\t- `◎ multi-repo` — session spans multiple repos (only available with `--repo all`)\n254\t- `● active` — session phase is `ACTIVE` or `IDLE` with `EndedAt == nil`\n255\t- `✓ committed` — checkpoint has a linked commit\n256\t\n257\t## Tool Time — Agent Insights\n258\t\n259\tTool-time breakdown is the primary metric on the `agents` tab. It answers \"how much time did the agent spend grepping vs conversing vs committing.\"\n260\t\n261\t### Categories\n262\t\n263\t8 categories, semantically colored:\n264\t\n265\t| Category | Mapping rule | Color (256) |\n266\t|---|---|---|\n267\t| `shell` | `Bash` | `179` |\n268\t| `fileOps` | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `NotebookEdit` | `75` |\n269\t| `search` | `Grep`, `Glob` | `81` |\n270\t| `mcp` | `mcp__*` | `170` |\n271\t| `agent` | `Agent`, `Skill` | `99` |\n272\t| `other` | everything else | `244` |\n273\t| `conversation` | assistant text time between tool_result and next tool_use | `250` |\n274\t| `commit` | `Bash` where command matches `^git (commit\\|push)` | `220` |\n275\t\n276\t`conversation` and `commit` are virtual categories:\n277\t\n278\t- `conversation` is a **sum of gaps** where the assistant produced text between a `tool_result` and the next `tool_use`. It does not overlap with any other category.\n279\t- `commit` is a **sub-bucket of shell**. Rendered as a secondary line under shell and summed separately (\"of which committing: 6m\"); not double-counted when categories are summed.\n280\t\n281\t### Derivation\n282\t\n283\tFor each assistant message containing `tool_use` content blocks, measure timestamps from the transcript JSONL:\n284\t\n285\t```\n286\tduration(tool_use_i) = timestamp(next tool_use OR turn end) − timestamp(tool_use_i)\n287\t```\n288\t\n289\tFor `conversation`:\n290\t\n291\t```\n292\tconversation_i = timestamp(next tool_use) − timestamp(tool_result_i)\n293\t                  counted only when assistant text was produced in the gap\n294\t```\n295\t\n296\t### Where Computation Lives\n297\t\n298\t- **For committed checkpoints** (tier 3): computed server-side by extending `extractToolMetrics` in `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts`. CLI consumes `toolProfile.categories[*].durationMs` from the api.\n299\t- **For active / un-pushed sessions** (tier 2): computed locally in the CLI by parsing the live transcript. Same algorithm, Go implementation, so the CLI can show tool-time for today's work before it's pushed.\n300\t\n301\tHonest labels: the UI calls this \"Time between tool calls\" or \"Session time by category.\" Not \"execution time\" — it includes agent thinking.\n302\t\n303\t### Rendering (agents tab)\n304\t\n305\t```\n306\t╭─ Tool time by agent (last 30d) ──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n307\t│ Claude Code   fileOps 2h 14m · shell 48m · conversation 1h 02m           │\n308\t│               search 22m · agent 18m · mcp 4m                            │\n309\t│               of which committing: 6m (11 commits)                       │\n310\t│                                                                            │\n311\t│ Codex         fileOps 38m · shell 14m · conversation 24m                 │\n312\t│               search 4m · agent 0 · mcp 0                                │\n313\t│               of which committing: 2m (3 commits)                        │\n314\t╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n315\t```\n316\t\n317\t## Focus Areas\n318\t\n319\tFocus areas are a required product signal. They determine which work clusters the user is spending time on.\n320\t\n321\t### Rule Source\n322\t\n323\tResolution order:\n324\t\n325\t1. repo-local config (`.entire/activity_areas.json`)\n326\t2. built-in rules (shipped with the CLI)\n327\t3. fallback path clustering (first meaningful repo-relative directory boundary)\n328\t\n329\tRepo-local config schema:\n330\t\n331\t```json\n332\t{\n333\t  \"version\": 1,\n334\t  \"areas\": [\n335\t    { \"match\": \"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/**\", \"label\": \"checkpoint storage\", \"priority\": 100 }\n336\t  ]\n337\t}\n338\t```\n339\t\n340\t### Matching Rules\n341\t\n342\t- highest priority wins\n343\t- ties broken by longest match\n344\t- fallback to first meaningful repo-relative directory boundary if no rule matches\n345\t\n346\t### Built-In Default Rules\n347\t\n348\tFor this repo (entireio/cli):\n349\t\n350\t- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/**` → `checkpoint storage`\n351\t- `cmd/entire/cli/session/**` → `session state`\n352\t- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/**` → `checkpoint strategy`\n353\t- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/**` → `agent integrations`\n354\t- `cmd/entire/cli/search**` → `search`\n355\t- `cmd/entire/cli/explain**` → `explain`\n356\t- `cmd/entire/cli/status**` → `status`\n357\t- `cmd/entire/cli/activity/**` → `activity`\n358\t- `cmd/entire/cli/trail/**` → `trails`\n359\t- `cmd/entire/cli/hooks**` → `hooks`\n360\t- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/**` → `integration tests`\n361\t- `e2e/**` → `e2e`\n362\t- `docs/architecture/**` → `architecture docs`\n363\t- `docs/**` → `docs`\n364\t\n365\t### Area Ranking\n366\t\n367\tDo not rank by file count.\n368\t\n369\tSession area score:\n370\t\n371\t- `4 × checkpoint_participation`\n372\t- `+1` if area appears in 2+ consecutive checkpoints\n373\t- `+1` if area appears in a linked-commit session\n374\t\n375\tRange area score:\n376\t\n377\t- `3 × session_participation`\n378\t- `3 × checkpoint_participation`\n379\t- `+1` if area appears across multiple repos (only with `--repo all`)\n380\t\n381\tRender only top 1–3 focus areas in summary surfaces.\n382\t\n383\t## Reuse Inventory\n384\t\n385\tWhat we ride on, not rebuild:\n386\t\n387\t### CLI-side (already in repo)\n388\t\n389\t| Need | Reuse | Location |\n390\t|---|---|---|\n391\t| List all active sessions | `strategy.ListSessionStates(ctx)` | `strategy/session_state.go:95` |\n392\t| Load one session | `strategy.LoadSessionState(ctx, id)` | `strategy/session_state.go:43` |\n393\t| List committed checkpoints | `strategy.ListCheckpoints(ctx)` | `strategy/common.go:122` |\n394\t| Per-checkpoint metadata | `checkpoint.CheckpointSummary`, `CommittedMetadata`, `InitialAttribution` | `checkpoint/checkpoint.go` |\n395\t| Hook-provided session metrics | `checkpoint.SessionMetrics` | `checkpoint/checkpoint.go:489` |\n396\t| Parse checkpoint trailer | `trailers.ParseCheckpointTrailer` | `trailers/` |\n397\t| Repo root, path helpers | `paths.WorktreeRoot`, `paths.ToRelativePath` | `paths/paths.go` |\n398\t| Authenticated api client | `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient(insecureHTTP)` | `api_client.go` (pattern in `trail_cmd.go`) |\n399\t| Detect login state | `auth.LookupCurrentToken()` | `auth/store.go:71` |\n400\t| Accessible forms | `NewAccessibleForm`, `isAccessibleMode()` | `help.go` |\n401\t| Relative time | `timeAgo` (extract to `stringutil/time.go`) | `status.go` |\n402\t| JSON output shape | `writeSessionInfoJSON` | `sessions.go:349` |\n403\t| Pager pattern | `outputWithPager` | `explain.go:1556` |\n404\t| Subcommand registration | `newSessionsCmd` → list/info/stop pattern | `sessions.go:22` |\n405\t| Transcript parsing | `transcript.Line`, `ToolInput` types | `transcript/types.go` |\n406\t\n407\t### Server-side (entire.io) — consumed via `api.Client`\n408\t\n409\t| Need | Endpoint |\n410\t|---|---|\n411\t| Daily commit + checkpoint split | `GET /:org/:repo/overview/commit-stats?since&until` |\n412\t| Contributors | `GET /:org/:repo/overview/contributors?since&until` |\n413\t| PR stats | `GET /:org/:repo/overview/pr-stats?since&until&timeZone` |\n414\t| Per-checkpoint analysis (labels, blocks, toolProfile) | existing review/analysis endpoint |\n415\t| Canonical label taxonomy | `CHECKPOINT_LABELS` in `api/src/types.ts:593` |\n416\t| Tool category schema | `ToolProfile` in `api/src/types.ts` |\n417\t\n418\t## Upstream Dependencies\n419\t\n420\tThese are **optional enrichment** — v1 ships without them. CLI handles absence gracefully. File as separate PR on entire.io:\n421\t\n422\t1. Extend `toolProfile.categories[*]` to include `durationMs` alongside `count`, computed by updating `extractToolMetrics` in `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts` to walk transcript timestamps.\n423\t2. Add `session_span_ms` on committed sessions (server-side canonical value using transcript timestamps). Today the CLI computes span locally; when the server field lands, CLI switches to it for committed checkpoints for cross-surface consistency.\n424\t3. Add `conversation` and `commit` virtual categories to the server's `ToolProfile` schema.\n425\t\n426\tUntil (1)/(3) land: tool-time categories render `count` only, labeled \"Tool usage\" instead of \"Tool time.\"\n427\tUntil (2) lands: span time is tier-2 local-derived for all sessions.\n428\t\n429\t## Visual Language\n430\t\n431\t### Palette\n432\t\n433\tBase palette inherits from `status_style.go` + `search_tui.go`. New additions for activity:\n434\t\n435\t| Role | 256-color | Usage |\n436\t|---|---|---|\n437\t| Primary accent | `214` | Active tab, KPI values, primary titles |\n438\t| Violet | `99` | Modes panel |\n439\t| Teal | `36` | Focus areas panel |\n440\t| Green | `43` | Heatmap panel |\n441\t| Magenta | `170` | Agents panel |\n442\t| Amber | `214` | Recent / drill-down panels |\n443\t| Secondary text | `244` | Inactive tabs, labels |\n444\t| Tertiary text | `245` / `243` / `240` | Help keys, separators, borders |\n445\t| Body dim | `Faint` | Muted context |\n446\t\n447\t### Label colors (locked, semantic)\n448\t\n449\tSame color for same label in every panel, every view, every session card. Full 18-label mapping lives in `activity/styles.go`.\n450\t\n451\tTop 8 by expected volume:\n452\t\n453\t| Label | 256-color |\n454\t|---|---|\n455\t| `feature_build` | `42` green |\n456\t| `bug_fix` | `203` red |\n457\t| `refactor` | `220` yellow |\n458\t| `testing` | `170` magenta |\n459\t| `investigation` | `81` cyan |\n460\t| `performance` / `optimization` | `214` orange |\n461\t| `documentation` | `75` blue |\n462\t| `security_fix` | `197` hot pink |\n463\t\n464\t### Heatmap — 5-tier ramp\n465\t\n466\t```\n467\t░  237   no activity\n468\t▒   22   low\n469\t▓   28   mid\n470\t▓   34   high\n471\t█   46   peak\n472\t```\n473\t\n474\t`NO_COLOR=1` fallback: `░▒▓█` only, no color. Same cells, different visual weight.\n475\t\n476\t### Gradient horizontal bars\n477\t\n478\tPort of CodeBurn's `gradientColor(pct)` lerp using our palette (cyan `43` → amber `214` → orange `202`). Filled cells are `█`, unfilled are `░` at `237`.\n479\t\n480\t```\n481\tfileOps   ████████████████████▓░░░░░   2h 14m\n482\tshell     ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░      48m\n483\tsearch    ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░      22m\n484\t```\n485\t\n486\t### Intra-day activity strip (today tab)\n487\t\n488\t24-cell horizontal bar, one per hour, using `▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█` proportional height + amber gradient:\n489\t\n490\t```\n491\t 0h                        12h                         23h\n492\t ▁ ▂ ▁ · · · · · ▃ ▅ █ █   █ ▇ ▅ ▃ ▁ · · · ▁ ▂ ▁ ·\n493\t```\n494\t\n495\t### Badges\n496\t\n497\tUnicode geometry only. No emoji in v1.\n498\t\n499\t```\n500\t⚑ linked   ↻ resumed   ⇢ delegated   ◎ multi-repo   ● active   ✓ committed\n501\t```\n502\t\n503\t### Borders\n504\t\n505\tRounded (`lipgloss.RoundedBorder()`) throughout, matching existing TUI code. Per-panel border color from palette above. 1x2 padding.\n506\t\n507\t### Fallbacks\n508\t\n509\t- `NO_COLOR=1`: no colors, keep density blocks and geometry.\n510\t- Piped output / non-tty: static renderer (no animation, no cursor, flat text).\n511\t- Narrow terminal (< 80 col): single-column stacked panels instead of grid.\n512\t- `ACCESSIBLE=1`: see Accessibility section.\n513\t\n514\t## Wireframes\n515\t\n516\t### Today tab (default view)\n517\t\n518\t```text\n519\t╭─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n520\t│  Entire Activity                                                             │\n521\t│                                                                              │\n522\t│   today   ·   range   ·   history   ·   agents   ·   repos   ·   report     │\n523\t│   ─────                                                                      │\n524\t│                                                                              │\n525\t│   repo: current  ·  profile: personal  ·  last: today                        │\n526\t╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n527\t\n528\t╭─ Today · Mon Apr 15 2026 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n529\t│ Sessions  3   Checkpoints  11   Linked  2   Span  2h 47m   Focus Areas  3   │\n530\t╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n531\t\n532\t╭─ Modes «99 violet» ─────────────╮  ╭─ Focus Areas «36 teal» ───────────────╮\n533\t│ ● feature_build  2              │  │ checkpoint storage  ████████▓  6      │\n534\t│ ● bug_fix        1              │  │ session state       ████░░░░░  3      │\n535\t│ ● testing        0              │  │ hooks               ██░░░░░░░  2     