file: observability ──────────────────────────────────────╮\n662\t│ Sessions  61   Checkpoints  184   Linked Rate  58%   Agents  3               │\n663\t╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n664\t\n665\t╭─ Heatmap «43 green» ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n666\t│ Jan                                                                      Mar │\n667\t│  · ░ ▒ █ · · ░ ░ █ ▒ · · ░ █ █ ▒ · · ░ ░ ▒ █ · · ░ ▒ █ ▒ ░ ·                 │\n668\t╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n669\t\n670\t╭─ Trends «99» ──────────────────╮  ╭─ Agent Mix Over Time «170» ───────────╮\n671\t│ Sessions / week                │  │ Claude Code      ████████            │\n672\t│ Checkpoints / week             │  │ Codex            ████                │\n673\t│ Linked commits / week          │  │ Cursor           ██                  │\n674\t╰─────────────────────────────────╯  ╰────────────────────────────────────────╯\n675\t\n676\t╭─ Outliers «214» ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n677\t│ Highest checkpoint density   2026-03-27   9 checkpoints in 42m              │\n678\t│ Longest span                 2026-04-03   2h 14m                            │\n679\t│ Most delegated session       2026-04-08   5 task checkpoints                │\n680\t╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n681\t```\n682\t\n683\t### Report tab\n684\t\n685\tProduces a shareable markdown/text report from the current range. Templates in v1:\n686\t\n687\t- `daily` — standup-format: \"Yesterday / Today / Notable checkpoints / Followups\"\n688\t- `weekly` — week summary aggregating top sessions + labels\n689\t\n690\tNice-to-have, not primary. Driven by `entire activity report --template <name> --format markdown|text`.\n691\t\n692\t## Accessibility\n693\t\n694\t`ACCESSIBLE=1` mode is a separate renderer, not a reformatted TUI.\n695\t\n696\tRules:\n697\t\n698\t- No box-drawing characters (`╭─╮│`).\n699\t- No heatmap grid — degrades to a per-day numeric table.\n700\t- No gradient bars — degrades to proportional bar using `=` characters with a numeric value.\n701\t- Sections use plain `H2`-style capitalized headers with a blank line.\n702\t- Nested data uses two-space indentation, not columns.\n703\t- Tab bar → linear H2 section per view.\n704\t- Drill-down → indented section under the selected session.\n705\t- Actions footer → list of real `entire ...` commands, copy-pasteable.\n706\t\n707\tExample (today tab):\n708\t\n709\t```text\n710\tEntire Activity — today\n711\tRepo: current · Profile: personal\n712\t\n713\tSummary\n714\t  Sessions: 3\n715\t  Checkpoints: 11\n716\t  Linked Commits: 2\n717\t  Span: 2h 47m\n718\t  Focus Areas: 3\n719\t\n720\tModes\n721\t  feature_build: 2\n722\t  bug_fix: 1\n723\t  testing: 0\n724\t\n725\tFocus Areas\n726\t  checkpoint storage: 6 checkpoints\n727\t  session state: 3 checkpoints\n728\t  hooks: 2 checkpoints\n729\t\n730\tRecent Sessions\n731\t  1. 09:12-10:06 — bug_fix — checkpoint storage, session state — linked commit\n732\t  2. 11:20-12:01 — feature_build — hooks, strategy — active\n733\t  3. 14:31-14:52 — testing — agent integrations — delegated\n734\t\n735\tTo drill into a session:\n736\t  entire activity today --session <session-id>\n737\t  entire explain --session <session-id>\n738\t```\n739\t\n740\tDetection: `os.Getenv(\"ACCESSIBLE\") != \"\"` or non-tty writer or `NO_COLOR` + narrow terminal.\n741\t\n742\t## Package Layout\n743\t\n744\tSlimmer than originally proposed. Classifier is out; file list is ~10-12.\n745\t\n746\tAdd `cmd/entire/cli/activity/`:\n747\t\n748\t- `model.go` — `ActivitySession`, `ActivityCheckpoint`, `ActivityDay`, summary types\n749\t- `load.go` — local loaders using `strategy.ListSessionStates` / `ListCheckpoints`\n750\t- `load_linked.go` — `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer lookup\n751\t- `enrich.go` — api enrichment (labels, toolProfile) with cache\n752\t- `focus_areas.go` — rule engine + built-ins + `.entire/activity_areas.json` loader\n753\t- `metrics.go` — aggregators (per-day, per-range, per-repo, per-agent)\n754\t- `heatmap.go` — heatmap cell binning\n755\t- `tool_time.go` — local transcript walker for active sessions\n756\t- `styles.go` — lipgloss styles, palette, label colors, gradient bar, heatmap ramp\n757\t- `tui_model.go` — bubbletea model, tab state\n758\t- `tui_panels.go` — panel renderers (KPI, modes, focus, heatmap, etc.)\n759\t- `tui_keys.go` — keyboard handling\n760\t- `static.go` — static renderer for non-tty / piped\n761\t- `json.go` — JSON output with `schema_version: \"v1\"`\n762\t- `report.go` — daily/weekly markdown templates\n763\t\n764\tCLI entrypoints (thin wrappers over the package):\n765\t\n766\t- `cmd/entire/cli/activity.go` — root + today (default)\n767\t- `cmd/entire/cli/activity_range.go`\n768\t- `cmd/entire/cli/activity_history.go`\n769\t- `cmd/entire/cli/activity_agents.go`\n770\t- `cmd/entire/cli/activity_repos.go`\n771\t- `cmd/entire/cli/activity_report.go`\n772\t\n773\tSmall shared refactor:\n774\t\n775\t- Extract `timeAgo` from `status.go` into `stringutil/time.go` so `activity` + `status` + `sessions` all share it.\n776\t\n777\t## JSON Output\n778\t\n779\tEvery `--json` response:\n780\t\n781\t```json\n782\t{\n783\t  \"schema_version\": \"v1\",\n784\t  \"generated_at\": \"2026-04-16T14:23:11Z\",\n785\t  \"scope\": { \"repo\": \"entireio/cli\", \"from\": \"2026-04-09\", \"to\": \"2026-04-16\" },\n786\t  \"sessions\": [ ... ],\n787\t  \"aggregates\": { ... }\n788\t}\n789\t```\n790\t\n791\tSchema versioning makes the output a stable contract. Downstream tools gate on `schema_version` before parsing.\n792\t\n793\t## Validation Plan\n794\t\n795\t### Data projection\n796\t\n797\t- Unit tests for `load.go` using in-memory fake session states and committed metadata. Assert the resulting `ActivitySession` fields match expectations.\n798\t- Table-driven tests for focus-area rule matching: priority, longest-match, fallback.\n799\t- Tests for `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer lookup against fixture git repos (use `testutil.InitRepo`).\n800\t\n801\t### Metrics\n802\t\n803\t- Session-span derivation across edge cases: single checkpoint, identical timestamps, missing timestamps.\n804\t- Heatmap bucketing across timezones.\n805\t- Streak calculation on sparse date sets (matches FE `useUserDashboardData.ts` behavior).\n806\t- Linked-commit rate with and without trailers.\n807\t\n808\t### Api enrichment\n809\t\n810\t- Mock `api.Client` returning `StoredCheckpointAnalysis` stubs.\n811\t- Cache hit / miss paths.\n812\t- Offline fallback: ensure no api calls when no token present.\n813\t- Pipeline version invalidation.\n814\t\n815\t### TUI\n816\t\n817\t- Snapshot tests for each tab's panel rendering at 80, 100, 160 cols.\n818\t- View switching, drill-down state, `ACCESSIBLE=1` fallback path.\n819\t\n820\t### Golden output\n821\t\n822\t- `--json` golden files per tab, frozen clock.\n823\t- Static renderer golden files per tab with `NO_COLOR=1`.\n824\t\n825\t## Risks\n826\t\n827\t- `--repo all` requires api access; offline users get single-repo only. Documented in `labels: offline · tip: ...` footer.\n828\t- Tool-time measurements include agent thinking (not pure exec time). Label explicitly as \"Time between tool calls.\"\n829\t- Commit-link lookup across long ranges can be slow. Mitigated by caching and lazy enrichment.\n830\t- Weak focus-area rules produce noisy summaries. Mitigated by repo-local `.entire/activity_areas.json` override.\n831\t- Dashboard density at 80 cols — narrow-mode stacked layout handles this.\n832\t\n833\t## Decisions (Locked)\n834\t\n835\t- Tabbed dashboard-first UI with 6 tabs.\n836\t- Local-first data model with lazy api enrichment; three-tier truth table.\n837\t- Sessions as containers, checkpoints as evidence; activity types are projections, never persisted.\n838\t- Repo is a first-class dimension; `--repo all` is default for logged-in users.\n839\t- No sprint framing, no file-churn leaderboard, no LLM prose in CLI.\n840\t- Server-authoritative labels via `StoredCheckpointAnalysis` (18-label multi-label taxonomy); no local classifier.\n841\t- Honest session span time via first-to-last checkpoint timestamp.\n842\t- Tool-time breakdown with 8 categories (6 tool + conversation + commit).\n843\t- Drill-down surfaces real `entire ...` commands as an Actions footer.\n844\t- `--json` includes `schema_version: \"v1\"` from day one.\n845\t- Visual language inherits lipgloss palette, extends with semantic label colors and per-panel borders.\n846\t- No emoji — Unicode geometry only.\n847\t- Upstream server changes (durationMs, session_span_ms) are optional enrichment, not v1 blockers.\n848\t"}]},"uuid":"97e0390b-8077-496f-9a11-191d8bb8aaad","timestamp":"2026-04-23T01:10:10.790Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/2026-04-15-entire-activity-design.md","content":"# Entire Activity Design\n\nDate: 2026-04-15 (revised 2026-04-16)\n\n## Summary\n\n`entire activity` is a new read-only product surface for understanding work captured by Entire over time.\n\nIt is centered on:\n\n- **sessions** as the primary unit of work\n- **checkpoints** as the evidence trail inside a session\n- **repo, time, and agent** as first-class grouping dimensions\n\nThis is not a sprint tool and should not use sprint language. It is an Entire-native activity layer over existing session, checkpoint, transcript, and commit-linkage data — rendered as a tabbed dashboard in the terminal.\n\n## Goals\n\n- Show what happened today and across selectable time ranges.\n- Make checkpoint and session activity easy to scan quickly.\n- Surface useful, defensible insights instead of generic churn metrics.\n- Support today / range / history / agents / repos / report tabs in v1.\n- Support interactive TUI and static output in v1.\n- Use only metrics that are directly available now or safely derivable from existing data.\n- Reuse existing CLI infrastructure (session state, checkpoint store, auth, lipgloss styles) rather than duplicating it.\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- No productivity score.\n- No “most modified files” leaderboard as a primary signal.\n- No sprint framing.\n- No LLM-generated prose in the CLI. (Server-side LLM classification is consumed as data, not re-generated locally.)\n- No claims of labor time or focus time beyond actual timestamp spans.\n- No local reimplementation of the server-side checkpoint analysis pipeline.\n\n## Product Definition\n\n`entire activity` answers:\n\n- what happened\n- when it happened\n- where it happened\n- what kind of work it was\n- which agents and models were involved\n- which checkpoints linked to commits\n- what should likely be resumed or finished\n\n## Information Architecture\n\nThe v1 surface is a **tabbed dashboard**. Six top-level tabs:\n\n```\ntoday │ range │ history │ agents │ repos │ report\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Each tab is a self-contained view with its own panel layout. Panels never span tabs.\n- Active tab is visually distinct (amber `214` with an underline rule); inactive tabs are faint gray `244`.\n- Keyboard: `1-6` jump directly to a tab. `tab` / `shift-tab` cycle. `q` quits.\n- Within a tab, arrow keys move between panels/rows. `enter` opens drill-down. `esc` closes drill-down.\n- CLI subcommands map 1:1 to tabs: `entire activity today` opens the today tab, `entire activity agents` opens agents tab, etc.\n\nProfiles only change defaults and emphasis (heatmap metric, whether token panels are prominent, etc.):\n\n- `personal` (default)\n- `team`\n- `observability`\n\n## Command Surface\n\n```bash\nentire activity                                 # opens TUI on 'today' tab\nentire activity today\nentire activity range --last 7d\nentire activity range --from 2026-04-01 --to 2026-04-15\nentire activity history\nentire activity agents\nentire activity repos\nentire activity report --template daily --format markdown\n```\n\nShared flags:\n\n```bash\n--repo current|owner/name|all|local\n--profile personal|team|observability\n--from YYYY-MM-DD\n--to YYYY-MM-DD\n--last 7d|14d|30d\n--group-by repo|day|agent\n--view cards|table\n--json\n--local-only    # never call the api; labels unavailable\n--no-color      # also honors NO_COLOR env var\n```\n\nNotes:\n\n- `entire activity` (no args) opens the TUI on the `today` tab.\n- `--repo all` is the default for logged-in users and covers every repo the user has api access to. `--repo current` narrows to the current worktree's repo. `--repo local` forces offline / this-repo-only mode.\n- All subcommands support static terminal output and JSON output.\n- `--json` output always includes `\"schema_version\": \"v1\"` at the top level.\n\n## Execution Model\n\n### Local-first, api-enriched\n\n- **Local is the default data source.** `entire activity today` with no login returns a complete, honest view of the current repo's activity using only local data.\n- **API enrichment is lazy.** When `entire login` has produced a token, the CLI fetches server-authoritative labels and tool-time data per checkpoint. Enrichment fills in asynchronously in the TUI and is batched before final print in static mode.\n- **Offline / not-logged-in fallback** is silent. Tab chrome shows a single line: `labels: offline · tip: run 'entire login' for agent insights`.\n- **Performance budget:**\n  - `today`: < 1s local, < 2s with api enrichment\n  - `range --last 7d`: < 3s local, < 6s with enrichment\n  - `range --last 30d`: < 6s local, < 12s with enrichment\n  - `history` (90d): < 10s local, < 30s with enrichment\n- **Cache** at `.git/entire-activity-cache/<checkpoint-id>.json` for api responses. Invalidated when `StoredCheckpointAnalysis.pipeline_version` changes.\n\n### Three-tier Data Truth Table\n\nEvery metric is sourced from exactly one tier. The UI tags metrics with their tier via the tab chrome footer (e.g. `labels: server · span: local · linked commits: local`).\n\n#### Tier 1 — Local-authoritative\n\nReadable from `.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json` (session state) and `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch (committed metadata):\n\n- session ID, checkpoint ID\n- session started / ended / last-interaction timestamps\n- session phase, step count\n- checkpoint timestamps\n- files touched per session / per checkpoint\n- base commit, worktree path, worktree ID\n- agent type, model name (when state records it)\n- token usage (when the agent or hook reports it)\n- prompt text (scoped per checkpoint)\n- attribution metadata (`InitialAttribution`)\n- `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer presence on user commits (via local `git log`)\n- hook-provided session metrics (`SessionMetrics.DurationMs/TurnCount/ContextTokens`) for agents that emit them (e.g., Cursor)\n\n#### Tier 2 — Local-derivable\n\nCheap computation from tier 1 with no api call:\n\n- **session span minutes** = `last_checkpoint_ts − first_checkpoint_ts` (honest first-to-last timestamp, replaces the FE `max(steps) × 2 / 60` estimate)\n- checkpoints per session, checkpoint density, median checkpoint gap\n- sessions/day, checkpoints/day\n- active day count, streaks (same algorithm as FE `useUserDashboardData.ts`)\n- heatmap cell intensity\n- intra-day hour buckets\n- resume-after-gap detection\n- focus area assignment from `files_touched` via rule engine\n- linked commit count, linked commit rate (via `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer lookup)\n- commit-linked vs exploratory-only split\n- badges (`resumed`, `linked commit`, `delegated`, `multi-repo`)\n- active-session rollups (un-pushed work that only exists locally)\n\n#### Tier 3 — Server-authoritative\n\nRequires `entire login` and a network round trip. Fetched per committed checkpoint and cached:\n\n- **work-mode labels** — `CheckpointExtraction.labels[]` from `StoredCheckpointAnalysis` (18-value multi-label taxonomy, max 3 per checkpoint)\n- **`toolProfile.categories[*].count`** — tool usage counts (shell / fileOps / search / mcp / agent / other)\n- **`toolProfile.categories[*].durationMs`** — tool time per category (**pending upstream server change**, see Upstream Dependencies)\n- `skillsUsed`, `mcpServersUsed`, `modelsUsed`, `agentsUsed`\n- execution feedback: `thrashing`, `bugProfile`, `architectureChanges`\n- cross-repo aggregation for `--repo all`\n- session span canonicalization (**pending** — until then CLI uses tier 2)\n\n## Core Data Model\n\nActivity types are **read-only projections**, not new primitives. They are built in `load.go` from existing `session.State` + `checkpoint.CheckpointSummary` + `checkpoint.CommittedMetadata` (+ optional api `StoredCheckpointAnalysis`). They are never persisted. The existing `session` and `checkpoint` packages remain the canonical owners of underlying data.\n\n### ActivitySession\n\nProjected from `session.State` + per-session checkpoint rollups. Key fields:\n\n- repo, session ID, branch (when available), worktree ID, worktree path\n- started at, ended at, last interaction at\n- span minutes (tier 2: honest, first→last checkpoint)\n- step count, task checkpoint count\n- checkpoints: `[]ActivityCheckpoint`\n- agents used, models used\n- focus areas (tier 2, from `files_touched`)\n- labels (tier 3, from api; empty when offline)\n- badges (tier 2, deterministic local)\n- token totals (tier 1 when available)\n- linked commit SHAs (tier 2)\n- is active, is resumable\n- `source` (local | server | mixed)\n\n### ActivityCheckpoint\n\nProjected from `checkpoint.CheckpointSummary` + `checkpoint.CommittedMetadata` (+ optional api). Key fields:\n\n- repo, session ID, checkpoint ID\n- timestamp\n- is task checkpoint, tool use ID\n- agent, model\n- focus areas (tier 2)\n- linked commit SHA (tier 2)\n- token usage (tier 1 when available)\n- turn ID\n- labels (tier 3, from api; empty when offline)\n- tool profile (tier 3, from api; empty when offline)\n- badges (tier 2)\n- source\n\n### ActivityDay\n\nPer-day rollup. Key fields: date, repos, sessions, checkpoints, task checkpoints, linked commits, token totals, label counts, focus area counts, resume count, tool-time totals (tier 3).\n\n### ActivityRangeSummary\n\nRange-level aggregates. Fields include: from, to, repos touched, sessions, checkpoints, task checkpoints, linked commits, active days, tokens, label counts (with confidence gating, see below), focus area counts, agent counts, model counts, repo summaries, top sessions, tool-time totals.\n\n### ActivityRepoSummary / ActivityAgentSummary\n\nRepo- and agent-scoped rollups used in `repos` and `agents` tabs.\n\n## Labels — Server-Authoritative\n\n### Why No Local Classifier\n\nThe entire.io api already runs `checkpoint-analysis-pipeline.ts` (pipeline version `2026-04-10.v3`) which uses the Anthropic SDK to produce `CheckpointExtraction { labels[], blocks[] }`. Results are stored as `StoredCheckpointAnalysis` in the db. This is the same pipeline that drives the web app's checkpoint summary UI (PR #1021).\n\nA second classifier in the CLI would produce a different taxonomy, different weights, and eventual drift. Users would see `build` in the TUI and `feature_build` in the web app for the same checkpoint — a reportable bug. We avoid that by letting the server own classification and having the CLI consume and render.\n\n### Canonical Taxonomy\n\nLabels are multi-label with max 3 per checkpoint, drawn from `CHECKPOINT_LABELS` in `api/src/types.ts`:\n\n```\nfeature_build, bug_fix, refactor, performance, optimization,\ninvestigation, configuration, testing, deployment, recovery,\nplanning, security_fix, documentation, migration, telemetry,\nobservability, enhancement, dependencies\n```\n\n### Rendering\n\n- Session cards and checkpoint rows show up to 3 label pills (semantic color per label; see Visual Language).\n- Sessions without a server analysis render **unlabeled**, not as `mixed`. Offline mode suppresses label pills entirely and notes it in the chrome footer.\n- Range-level \"modes\" panels aggregate by summing label occurrences across checkpoints/sessions.\n- A range never claims a dominant mode unless: top label share ≥ 0.55 and top leads runner-up by ≥ 0.15. Otherwise render `Modes: feature_build 4 · bug_fix 3 · testing 2`.\n\n## Badges — Local Deterministic\n\nBadges are cheap local facts, not classifications. They don't require the api.\n\n- `⚑ linked` — session has at least one `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer on an active-branch commit\n- `↻ resumed` — session started after ≥ 6h gap from the prior session on the same branch\n- `⇢ delegated` — session has task checkpoint count ≥ 1\n- `◎ multi-repo` — session spans multiple repos (only available with `--repo all`)\n- `● active` — session phase is `ACTIVE` or `IDLE` with `EndedAt == nil`\n- `✓ committed` — checkpoint has a linked commit\n\n## Tool Time — Agent Insights\n\nTool-time breakdown is the primary metric on the `agents` tab. It answers \"how much time did the agent spend grepping vs conversing vs committing.\"\n\n### Categories\n\n8 categories, semantically colored:\n\n| Category | Mapping rule | Color (256) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `shell` | `Bash` | `179` |\n| `fileOps` | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `NotebookEdit` | `75` |\n| `search` | `Grep`, `Glob` | `81` |\n| `mcp` | `mcp__*` | `170` |\n| `agent` | `Agent`, `Skill` | `99` |\n| `other` | everything else | `244` |\n| `conversation` | assistant text time between tool_result and next tool_use | `250` |\n| `commit` | `Bash` where command matches `^git (commit\\|push)` | `220` |\n\n`conversation` and `commit` are virtual categories:\n\n- `conversation` is a **sum of gaps** where the assistant produced text between a `tool_result` and the next `tool_use`. It does not overlap with any other category.\n- `commit` is a **sub-bucket of shell**. Rendered as a secondary line under shell and summed separately (\"of which committing: 6m\"); not double-counted when categories are summed.\n\n### Derivation\n\nFor each assistant message containing `tool_use` content blocks, measure timestamps from the transcript JSONL:\n\n```\nduration(tool_use_i) = timestamp(next tool_use OR turn end) − timestamp(tool_use_i)\n```\n\nFor `conversation`:\n\n```\nconversation_i = timestamp(next tool_use) − timestamp(tool_result_i)\n                  counted only when assistant text was produced in the gap\n```\n\n### Where Computation Lives\n\n- **For committed checkpoints** (tier 3): computed server-side by extending `extractToolMetrics` in `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts`. CLI consumes `toolProfile.categories[*].durationMs` from the api.\n- **For active / un-pushed sessions** (tier 2): computed locally in the CLI by parsing the live transcript. Same algorithm, Go implementation, so the CLI can show tool-time for today's work before it's pushed.\n\nHonest labels: the UI calls this \"Time between tool calls\" or \"Session time by category.\" Not \"execution time\" — it includes agent thinking.\n\n### Rendering (agents tab)\n\n```\n╭─ Tool time by agent (last 30d) ──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ Claude Code   fileOps 2h 14m · shell 48m · conversation 1h 02m           │\n│               search 22m · agent 18m · mcp 4m                            │\n│               of which committing: 6m (11 commits)                       │\n│                                                                            │\n│ Codex         fileOps 38m · shell 14m · conversation 24m                 │\n│               search 4m · agent 0 · mcp 0                                │\n│               of which committing: 2m (3 commits)                        │\n╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n```\n\n## Focus Areas\n\nFocus areas are a required product signal. They determine which work clusters the user is spending time on.\n\n### Rule Source\n\nResolution order:\n\n1. repo-local config (`.entire/activity_areas.json`)\n2. built-in rules (shipped with the CLI)\n3. fallback path clustering (first meaningful repo-relative directory boundary)\n\nRepo-local config schema:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"areas\": [\n    { \"match\": \"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/**\", \"label\": \"checkpoint storage\", \"priority\": 100 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Matching Rules\n\n- highest priority wins\n- ties broken by longest match\n- fallback to first meaningful repo-relative directory boundary if no rule matches\n\n### Built-In Default Rules\n\nFor this repo (entireio/cli):\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/**` → `checkpoint storage`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/session/**` → `session state`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/**` → `checkpoint strategy`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/**` → `agent integrations`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search**` → `search`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain**` → `explain`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/status**` → `status`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/activity/**` → `activity`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/trail/**` → `trails`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/hooks**` → `hooks`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/**` → `integration tests`\n- `e2e/**` → `e2e`\n- `docs/architecture/**` → `architecture docs`\n- `docs/**` → `docs`\n\n### Area Ranking\n\nDo not rank by file count.\n\nSession area score:\n\n- `4 × checkpoint_participation`\n- `+1` if area appears in 2+ consecutive checkpoints\n- `+1` if area appears in a linked-commit session\n\nRange area score:\n\n- `3 × session_participation`\n- `3 × checkpoint_participation`\n- `+1` if area appears across multiple repos (only with `--repo all`)\n\nRender only top 1–3 focus areas in summary surfaces.\n\n## Reuse Inventory\n\nWhat we ride on, not rebuild:\n\n### CLI-side (already in repo)\n\n| Need | Reuse | Location |\n|---|---|---|\n| List all active sessions | `strategy.ListSessionStates(ctx)` | `strategy/session_state.go:95` |\n| Load one session | `strategy.LoadSessionState(ctx, id)` | `strategy/session_state.go:43` |\n| List committed checkpoints | `strategy.ListCheckpoints(ctx)` | `strategy/common.go:122` |\n| Per-checkpoint metadata | `checkpoint.CheckpointSummary`, `CommittedMetadata`, `InitialAttribution` | `checkpoint/checkpoint.go` |\n| Hook-provided session metrics | `checkpoint.SessionMetrics` | `checkpoint/checkpoint.go:489` |\n| Parse checkpoint trailer | `trailers.ParseCheckpointTrailer` | `trailers/` |\n| Repo root, path helpers | `paths.WorktreeRoot`, `paths.ToRelativePath` | `paths/paths.go` |\n| Authenticated api client | `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient(insecureHTTP)` | `api_client.go` (pattern in `trail_cmd.go`) |\n| Detect login state | `auth.LookupCurrentToken()` | `auth/store.go:71` |\n| Accessible forms | `NewAccessibleForm`, `isAccessibleMode()` | `help.go` |\n| Relative time | `timeAgo` (extract to `stringutil/time.go`) | `status.go` |\n| JSON output shape | `writeSessionInfoJSON` | `sessions.go:349` |\n| Pager pattern | `outputWithPager` | `explain.go:1556` |\n| Subcommand registration | `newSessionsCmd` → list/info/stop pattern | `sessions.go:22` |\n| Transcript parsing | `transcript.Line`, `ToolInput` types | `transcript/types.go` |\n\n### Server-side (entire.io) — consumed via `api.Client`\n\n| Need | Endpoint |\n|---|---|\n| Daily commit + checkpoint split | `GET /:org/:repo/overview/commit-stats?since&until` |\n| Contributors | `GET /:org/:repo/overview/contributors?since&until` |\n| PR stats | `GET /:org/:repo/overview/pr-stats?since&until&timeZone` |\n| Per-checkpoint analysis (labels, blocks, toolProfile) | existing review/analysis endpoint |\n| Canonical label taxonomy | `CHECKPOINT_LABELS` in `api/src/types.ts:593` |\n| Tool category schema | `ToolProfile` in `api/src/types.ts` |\n\n## Upstream Dependencies\n\nThese are **optional enrichment** — v1 ships without them. CLI handles absence gracefully. File as separate PR on entire.io:\n\n1. Extend `toolProfile.categories[*]` to include `durationMs` alongside `count`, computed by updating `extractToolMetrics` in `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts` to walk transcript timestamps.\n2. Add `session_span_ms` on committed sessions (server-side canonical value using transcript timestamps). Today the CLI computes span locally; when the server field lands, CLI switches to it for committed checkpoints for cross-surface consistency.\n3. Add `conversation` and `commit` virtual categories to the server's `ToolProfile` schema.\n\nUntil (1)/(3) land: tool-time categories render `count` only, labeled \"Tool usage\" instead of \"Tool time.\"\nUntil (2) lands: span time is tier-2 local-derived for all sessions.\n\n## Visual Language\n\n### Palette\n\nBase palette inherits from `status_style.go` + `search_tui.go`. New additions for activity:\n\n| Role | 256-color | Usage |\n|---|---|---|\n| Primary accent | `214` | Active tab, KPI values, primary titles |\n| Violet | `99` | Modes panel |\n| Teal | `36` | Focus areas panel |\n| Green | `43` | Heatmap panel |\n| Magenta | `170` | Agents panel |\n| Amber | `214` | Recent / drill-down panels |\n| Secondary text | `244` | Inactive tabs, labels |\n| Tertiary text | `245` / `243` / `240` | Help keys, separators, borders |\n| Body dim | `Faint` | Muted context |\n\n### Label colors (locked, semantic)\n\nSame color for same label in every panel, every view, every session card. Full 18-label mapping lives in `activity/styles.go`.\n\nTop 8 by expected volume:\n\n| Label | 256-color |\n|---|---|\n| `feature_build` | `42` green |\n| `bug_fix` | `203` red |\n| `refactor` | `220` yellow |\n| `testing` | `170` magenta |\n| `investigation` | `81` cyan |\n| `performance` / `optimization` | `214` orange |\n| `documentation` | `75` blue |\n| `security_fix` | `197` hot pink |\n\n### Heatmap — 5-tier ramp\n\n```\n░  237   no activity\n▒   22   low\n▓   28   mid\n▓   34   high\n█   46   peak\n```\n\n`NO_COLOR=1` fallback: `░▒▓█` only, no color. Same cells, different visual weight.\n\n### Gradient horizontal bars\n\nPort of CodeBurn's `gradientColor(pct)` lerp using our palette (cyan `43` → amber `214` → orange `202`). Filled cells are `█`, unfilled are `░` at `237`.\n\n```\nfileOps   ████████████████████▓░░░░░   2h 14m\nshell     ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░      48m\nsearch    ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░      22m\n```\n\n### Intra-day activity strip (today tab)\n\n24-cell horizontal bar, one per hour, using `▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█` proportional height + amber gradient:\n\n```\n 0h                        12h                         23h\n ▁ ▂ ▁ · · · · · ▃ ▅ █ █   █ ▇ ▅ ▃ ▁ · · · ▁ ▂ ▁ ·\n```\n\n### Badges\n\nUnicode geometry only. No emoji in v1.\n\n```\n⚑ linked   ↻ resumed   ⇢ delegated   ◎ multi-repo   ● active   ✓ committed\n```\n\n### Borders\n\nRounded (`lipgloss.RoundedBorder()`) throughout, matching existing TUI code. Per-panel border color from palette above. 1x2 padding.\n\n### Fallbacks\n\n- `NO_COLOR=1`: no colors, keep density blocks and geometry.\n- Piped output / non-tty: static renderer (no animation, no cursor, flat text).\n- Narrow terminal (< 80 col): single-column stacked panels instead of grid.\n- `ACCESSIBLE=1`: see Accessibility section.\n\n## Wireframes\n\n### Today tab (default view)\n\n```text\n╭─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│  Entire Activity                                                             │\n│                                                                              │\n│   today   ·   range   ·   history   ·   agents   ·   repos   ·   report     │\n│   ─────                                                                      │\n│                                                                              │\n│   repo: current  ·  profile: personal  ·  last: today                        │\n╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n╭─ Today · Mon Apr 15 2026 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ Sessions  3   Checkpoints  11   Linked  2   Span  2h 47m   Focus Areas  3   │\n╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n╭─ Modes «99 violet» ─────────────╮  ╭─ Focus Areas «36 teal» ───────────────╮\n│ ● feature_build  2              │  │ checkpoint storage  ████████▓  6      │\n│ ● bug_fix        1              │  │ session state       ████░░░░░  3      │\n│ ● testing        0              │  │ hooks               ██░░░░░░░  2      │\n╰─────────────────────────────────╯  ╰────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n╭─ Activity «43 green» ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│  0h                        12h                         23h                  │\n│  ░ ░ ░ · · · · · ▃ ▅ █ █   █ ▇ ▅ ▃ ▁ · · · ▁ ▂ ▁ ·                           │\n│                                                                               │\n│  Mar 24  25  26  27  28  29  30                                              │\n│  Apr 31   1   2   3   4   5   6                                              │\n│        ░   ▒   ▓   █   ▒   ░   ░                                             │\n│  Apr  7   8   9  10  11  12  13                                              │\n│        ▒   █   █   ▓   ▒   █   ▓                                             │\n╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n╭─ Recent Sessions «214 amber» ────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ 09:12-10:06  ● bug_fix        checkpoint storage + session state  ⚑ linked   │\n│ 11:20-12:01  ● feature_build  hooks + strategy                    ● active   │\n│ 14:31-14:52  ● testing        agent integrations                  ⇢ delegated│\n╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n  labels: offline · tip: run 'entire login' for agent insights\n  1 today  2 range  3 history  4 agents  5 repos  6 report  ·  q quit\n```\n\n### Drill-down (overlay on a tab)\n\nOpened with `enter` on a session row.\n\n```text\n╭─ Session: 2026-04-15-abc... · 11:20-12:01 ───────────────────────────────────╮\n│ Agent: Claude Code    Model: sonnet                                          │\n│ Labels: ● feature_build  ● testing                      