{"parentUuid":"e4731c4f-0a0c-4b8e-8287-8c3849a3135c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014Z75mC6RhoHJruukar1bb2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YYeh7q1GeiAU6Pks28GXoQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/2026-04-21-entire-activity-replan.md","content":"# Entire Activity Replan\n\nDate: 2026-04-21\nSupersedes: `docs/2026-04-15-entire-activity-design.md` (6-tab, local-aggregation design)\n\n## Premise\n\nTwo server endpoints now cover 90% of what `entire activity` needs to show:\n\n- `GET /api/v1/me/activity` — stats, `daily_contributions`, `hourly_contributions`, repo breakdown (PR #1590 landed)\n- `GET /api/v1/me/recap` — per-agent checkpoints / tokens / labels / skills / mcpServers / toolMix, with optional contributors column when `?repo=` is set (in review on `feat/me-recap-endpoint`)\n\nEverything else is already local: session state (`.git/entire-sessions/`), checkpoints (`entire/checkpoints/v1`), tool-time walker (commits `7560cd2…646625fc`). The CLI is a renderer, not an aggregator.\n\nReplan goal: collapse the old 6-tab dashboard into **3 tabs** that map 1:1 to those data sources, and delete the local-aggregation code it obsoletes.\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- No new server endpoints. If a metric isn't in `/me/activity` or `/me/recap`, cut it.\n- No local classifier, no focus-area rule engine, no heatmap binning in the CLI. Charts render what the server sends.\n- No `report` / `history` tabs in v1. Postpone.\n- No rename back to `activity/` package yet — the package stays `recap/` until the command is renamed in Chunk 3.\n\n## Three Tabs\n\n| Tab | Source | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| **overview** | `GET /me/activity` | KPI bar (sessions, checkpoints, linked, streak), 7-day bar, 24-hour strip, active-sessions tail (local) |\n| **agents** | `GET /me/recap` + local tool-time | Per-agent row: checkpoints, tokens, top labels, top skills, toolMix bars, `of which committing:` |\n| **repos** | `/me/activity.repos` | Per-repo card: total + per-agent contribution counts |\n\nKeyboard: `1/2/3` jump, `tab`/`shift-tab` cycle, `←/→` range (day/week/30d/90d), `q` quits. Range selector lives in the header, not per-tab.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n```\nentire activity\n  └── fetchMeActivity(timeframe, tz)  ─┐\n  └── fetchMeRecap(timeframe, repo)   ─┤── one model ─> three tab renderers\n  └── localActiveSessions()           ─┘\n```\n\n- Both server calls run in parallel from the bubbletea `Init` command.\n- Local active-session scan is synchronous (cheap) — used only on the overview tab for un-pushed work.\n- Tool-time for active sessions uses the per-agent `WalkToolCalls` walkers (already merged); committed-checkpoint tool-time comes from `toolMix` on the recap response.\n- No cache layer in v1. Endpoints are cheap; reopening the TUI re-fetches. Cache can come later if measured.\n\n## Scope Cuts (vs. 2026-04-15 design)\n\nDelete or skip:\n\n- `recap/heatmap.go` — 7-day bar and 24-hour strip render from `daily_contributions` / `hourly_contributions` directly; no binning needed.\n- `recap/badges.go` — badges were a tier-2 local derivation. Keep `● active` only; cut the rest.\n- `recap/insights.go` — \"dominant mode\" gating logic belongs server-side if at all.\n- Six-tab TUI → three-tab TUI. Drill-down overlay postponed.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/activity_{range,history,agents,repos,report}.go` entrypoints — one binary, `entire activity`.\n- `--profile personal|team|observability` flag — unused in a 3-tab view.\n- `--json` schema_version — keep, but only for overview+agents. Repos tab is a subset.\n\nKeep:\n\n- `recap/load.go`, `load_linked.go`, `load_checkpoints.go` — active-session rollup for overview's tail.\n- `recap/styles.go`, `render_chart.go`, `render_panel.go` — visual primitives.\n- `recap/agents_card.go` — already wired for me + contributors columns.\n- `recap/me_recap.go` — the client for `/me/recap`.\n\n## File Structure\n\n| File | Role | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/activity.go` | Cobra entrypoint, flag parsing, TUI launch | **new** (replaces `recap.go` once we're confident) |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/me_activity.go` | Client for `GET /me/activity` (mirrors `me_recap.go`) | **new** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go` | 3-tab bubbletea model | **rewrite** (currently single-view) |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/overview_panel.go` | KPI row + 7-day bar + 24h strip + active tail | **new** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/repos_panel.go` | Repo card list | **new** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/agents_card.go` | Per-agent rows | keep |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_chart.go` | Bars + strips | keep |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/{heatmap,insights,badges}.go` | Local aggregation | **delete** |\n\nPackage rename (`recap/` → `activity/`) is a separate PR after the command flips.\n\n## Chunks\n\n### Chunk 1: Server client for `/me/activity`\n\n- Add `cmd/entire/cli/recap/me_activity.go` — `FetchMeActivity(ctx, client, timeframe, tz, limit) (*ActivityResponse, error)` mirroring the shape in `api/src/routes/me.ts:133-163`.\n- Tests against a `httptest.Server` returning golden JSON from the endpoint's zod schema.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): client for GET /me/activity`.\n\n### Chunk 2: 3-tab TUI shell\n\n- Rewrite `recap/tui.go` — `type model struct { tab int; overview, agents, repos *tabState; range_ RangeKey }`.\n- Wire `1/2/3`, `tab`, `←/→`, `q`. Header shows range + timeframe + loading spinner per tab.\n- Skeleton panel files return placeholder text; fetch commands dispatch both endpoints in parallel.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): 3-tab TUI shell with parallel fetch`.\n\n### Chunk 3: Overview panel\n\n- KPI row from `response.stats` (tasks, orchestration, iteration, throughput, streak, current_streak).\n- 7-day bar aggregating `daily_contributions` server-side (already summed per agent); render with the existing `render_chart.go` gradient bar.\n- 24-hour strip from `hourly_contributions` keyed to local tz (the endpoint already bucketed in the caller-supplied tz).\n- Active-sessions tail: reuse `recap/load.go` for un-pushed sessions only; 3-row limit.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): overview tab`.\n\n### Chunk 4: Agents panel\n\n- Consume `/me/recap` response; render one row per agent via `agents_card.go`.\n- Overlay local tool-time for active sessions (WalkToolCalls walkers) onto the \"me\" column; contributors column is server-only.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): agents tab wired to /me/recap`.\n\n### Chunk 5: Repos panel\n\n- Consume `response.repos` from `/me/activity`. One card per repo: total count + 3 top agent counts.\n- No drill-down; selecting a repo later can narrow `/me/recap?repo=` — postpone.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): repos tab`.\n\n### Chunk 6: Command rename + cleanup\n\n- Add `entire activity` cobra command; keep `entire recap` as a hidden alias for one release.\n- Delete `recap/{heatmap,insights,badges}.go` + tests.\n- Update `--help`, README snippet, e2e canary prompts.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): rename entire recap to entire activity`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit: each fetch client against `httptest.Server`. Each panel against a frozen response fixture (golden string assertion at 80/120 col widths).\n- Integration: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/` — run `entire activity --json` against a mock server, assert `schema_version: \"v1\"` and shape.\n- E2E: no new canary — the Vogon agent doesn't exercise network endpoints. Manual smoke: `ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787 entire activity --insecure-http-auth`.\n\n## Risks\n\n- `/me/recap` hasn't merged yet. Chunk 4 blocks on that PR. Chunks 1-3 can land independently.\n- `hourly_contributions` is bucketed in a caller-supplied tz; the CLI must pass the user's IANA tz (`time.Local.String()` gives it on most systems). Fall back to `UTC` with a footer note.\n- Deleting `heatmap.go` removes the 90-day grid. If the server later grows a `/me/activity/heatmap` endpoint, re-add as a 4th tab, not inline.\n\n## Open Questions (non-blocking)\n\n- Should the range selector push `timeframe=` to both endpoints, or let each tab set its own? **Propose:** single global range, refetch both on change.\n- Do we want a `--repo=current` filter in v1? **Propose:** yes — `/me/recap?repo=` already supports it; `/me/activity` does not, so the repos tab stays cross-repo.\n- Is `recap` package rename worth a dedicated PR? **Propose:** yes, after Chunk 6, to keep diffs reviewable.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":777,"cache_read_input_tokens":85590,"output_tokens":3848,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":777,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3848,"cache_read_input_tokens":85590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":777},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKpD9FVAqviDGtagcZ9j","type":"assistant","uuid":"071c98d9-35b2-4b12-bbf5-d200d8276aa3","timestamp":"2026-04-23T01:13:57.858Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"kind-beaming-shannon"}
