go`, `load_checkpoints.go` — active-session rollup for overview's tail.\n- `recap/styles.go`, `render_chart.go`, `render_panel.go` — visual primitives.\n- `recap/agents_card.go` — already wired for me + contributors columns.\n- `recap/me_recap.go` — the client for `/me/recap`.\n\n## File Structure\n\n| File | Role | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/activity.go` | Cobra entrypoint, flag parsing, TUI launch | **new** (replaces `recap.go` once we're confident) |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/me_activity.go` | Client for `GET /me/activity` (mirrors `me_recap.go`) | **new** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go` | 3-tab bubbletea model | **rewrite** (currently single-view) |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/overview_panel.go` | KPI row + 7-day bar + 24h strip + active tail | **new** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/repos_panel.go` | Repo card list | **new** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/agents_card.go` | Per-agent rows | keep |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_chart.go` | Bars + strips | keep |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/{heatmap,insights,badges}.go` | Local aggregation | **delete** |\n\nPackage rename (`recap/` → `activity/`) is a separate PR after the command flips.\n\n## Chunks\n\n### Chunk 1: Server client for `/me/activity`\n\n- Add `cmd/entire/cli/recap/me_activity.go` — `FetchMeActivity(ctx, client, timeframe, tz, limit) (*ActivityResponse, error)` mirroring the shape in `api/src/routes/me.ts:133-163`.\n- Tests against a `httptest.Server` returning golden JSON from the endpoint's zod schema.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): client for GET /me/activity`.\n\n### Chunk 2: 3-tab TUI shell\n\n- Rewrite `recap/tui.go` — `type model struct { tab int; overview, agents, repos *tabState; range_ RangeKey }`.\n- Wire `1/2/3`, `tab`, `←/→`, `q`. Header shows range + timeframe + loading spinner per tab.\n- Skeleton panel files return placeholder text; fetch commands dispatch both endpoints in parallel.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): 3-tab TUI shell with parallel fetch`.\n\n### Chunk 3: Overview panel\n\n- KPI row from `response.stats` (tasks, orchestration, iteration, throughput, streak, current_streak).\n- 7-day bar aggregating `daily_contributions` server-side (already summed per agent); render with the existing `render_chart.go` gradient bar.\n- 24-hour strip from `hourly_contributions` keyed to local tz (the endpoint already bucketed in the caller-supplied tz).\n- Active-sessions tail: reuse `recap/load.go` for un-pushed sessions only; 3-row limit.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): overview tab`.\n\n### Chunk 4: Agents panel\n\n- Consume `/me/recap` response; render one row per agent via `agents_card.go`.\n- Overlay local tool-time for active sessions (WalkToolCalls walkers) onto the \"me\" column; contributors column is server-only.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): agents tab wired to /me/recap`.\n\n### Chunk 5: Repos panel\n\n- Consume `response.repos` from `/me/activity`. One card per repo: total count + 3 top agent counts.\n- No drill-down; selecting a repo later can narrow `/me/recap?repo=` — postpone.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): repos tab`.\n\n### Chunk 6: Command rename + cleanup\n\n- Add `entire activity` cobra command; keep `entire recap` as a hidden alias for one release.\n- Delete `recap/{heatmap,insights,badges}.go` + tests.\n- Update `--help`, README snippet, e2e canary prompts.\n- Commit: `feat(activity): rename entire recap to entire activity`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit: each fetch client against `httptest.Server`. Each panel against a frozen response fixture (golden string assertion at 80/120 col widths).\n- Integration: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/` — run `entire activity --json` against a mock server, assert `schema_version: \"v1\"` and shape.\n- E2E: no new canary — the Vogon agent doesn't exercise network endpoints. Manual smoke: `ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787 entire activity --insecure-http-auth`.\n\n## Risks\n\n- `/me/recap` hasn't merged yet. Chunk 4 blocks on that PR. Chunks 1-3 can land independently.\n- `hourly_contributions` is bucketed in a caller-supplied tz; the CLI must pass the user's IANA tz (`time.Local.String()` gives it on most systems). Fall back to `UTC` with a footer note.\n- Deleting `heatmap.go` removes the 90-day grid. If the server later grows a `/me/activity/heatmap` endpoint, re-add as a 4th tab, not inline.\n\n## Open Questions (non-blocking)\n\n- Should the range selector push `timeframe=` to both endpoints, or let each tab set its own? **Propose:** single global range, refetch both on change.\n- Do we want a `--repo=current` filter in v1? **Propose:** yes — `/me/recap?repo=` already supports it; `/me/activity` does not, so the repos tab stays cross-repo.\n- Is `recap` package rename worth a dedicated PR? **Propose:** yes, after Chunk 6, to keep diffs reviewable.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"071c98d9-35b2-4b12-bbf5-d200d8276aa3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"kind-beaming-shannon"}
