{"parentUuid":"6a76bc67-0da4-47b5-ae37-5bf72ac449f6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KCCXJRpzSQPuALnzQ89m76","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnosed. The 401 isn't the token format — it's that your `ent_...` token is in the **production** D1 database, but wrangler dev uses a **local** D1 at `.wrangler/state/v3/d1/`. The middleware does `db.apiTokens.findByTokenHash(sha256(token))` (line 196) and the local DB has zero rows, so the lookup fails at line 199 → \"Not authenticated.\"\n\nTwo paths forward — pick whichever matches your intent:\n\n### Path A — seed a token into local D1 (fastest to test)\n\nHash your prod token and insert a row so the local DB recognizes it. Paste in a second fish tab (wrangler stays running):\n\n```fish\nset RAW (security find-generic-password -s entire-cli -a \"https://entire.io\" -w)\nset TOKEN (string replace \"go-keyring-base64:\" \"\" -- $RAW | base64 -d)\nset HASH (echo -n $TOKEN | shasum -a 256 | awk '{print $1}')\necho \"Token hash: $HASH\"\n```\n\nThen in the same terminal, from `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint/api`:\n\n```fish\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint/api\n# First: find your user_id in local D1 (or seed one)\nbunx wrangler d1 execute entireio-db --local --command \"SELECT id FROM users LIMIT 1\"\n# Then insert the api_token row with the hash above and that user_id\nbunx wrangler d1 execute entireio-db --local --command \"INSERT INTO api_tokens (id, user_id, token_hash, name, expires_at, created_at) VALUES ('dev-1', '<user-id-from-above>', '<HASH>', 'local-dev', datetime('now', '+1 year'), datetime('now'))\"\n```\n\nIf the local users table is empty, this won't work — you need at least one user row. That means Path B.\n\n### Path B — log in against localhost (recommended, tests the full stack)\n\n```fish\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity\nenv ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787 go run ./cmd/entire login --insecure-http-auth\n```\n\nThis runs the device-auth flow against your local wrangler, which walks through OAuth to GitHub, creates a user row in local D1, and writes a new token keyed to `http://localhost:8787` in your keychain. After that:\n\n```fish\nenv ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787 go run ./cmd/entire recap --insecure-http-auth --week --repo entireio/cli\n```\n\nwill hit `/me/recap` with a valid local token — proving the endpoint end-to-end.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThis is a common gotcha with Cloudflare Workers local dev: `.dev.vars` gives you secrets that match prod, but **bindings** (D1, KV, Durable Objects, R2) are locally simulated by default. So JWT-signed stuff works cross-environment, but anything backed by a binding query (which is the majority of auth checks) needs fresh local data. It's why `wrangler dev --remote` exists — that flag points at real prod bindings, but you almost never want that for development.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nMy recommendation: **Path B**. It tests the actual flow a user hits and populates local D1 in the process, which you'll need for iterating on the endpoint anyway."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":102649,"output_tokens":2161,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2161,"cache_read_input_tokens":102649,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKtSK8dtw6Q2rQMAA41c","type