{"parentUuid":"5ceb8b26-abe7-412c-b47d-0161793a7c6e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ThyR9LguwNZni9gsQfNeEx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — tokens is 1 of 8 fields on each side. Per agent, per side (me / contributors), the endpoint returns:\n\n| Field | Source | Tier |\n|---|---|---|\n| `checkpoints` | `repo_checkpoints` row count | deterministic |\n| `transcriptTokens` | sum of transcript token counts | deterministic |\n| `filesChanged` | sum from `repo_commits.files_changed` | deterministic |\n| `tokens` | contributors only (me side is intentionally 0) | deterministic |\n| `labels` | `CheckpointExtraction.labels[]` from analyses | LLM-dependent |\n| `skills` | `skillsUsed` from analyses | LLM-dependent |\n| `mcpServers` | `mcpServersUsed` from analyses | LLM-dependent |\n| `toolMix` | `toolProfile.categories` from analyses | LLM-dependent |\n\nThe top 4 survive with the LLM pipeline off. The bottom 4 require `repo_checkpoint_analyses` to be populated (which is why they're empty locally).\n\nSo the endpoint's real job is **one call replaces three**:\n- `GET /me/checkpoints` (list)\n- `POST /checkpoints/analyses/batch` (per-checkpoint analyses)\n- `GET /:org/:repo/overview/*` (contributor rollup)\n\n…and it stitches per-agent on the server instead of making the CLI do client-side joining. Tokens is just one dimension of that; it's listed in the payload but the design note says the CLI should overwrite it from local metadata, so in practice it's noise in the me-side response.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe reason tokens sits in the payload at all is pure schema symmetry: same shape on me and contributors sides keeps the CLI rendering code uniform. If we dropped `tokens` from me, the CLI would need a conditional render — \"if contributors, show tokens column; if me, hide it.\" Symmetry costs a zeroed field; asymmetry costs a branch in every renderer. The 8-field payload chose symmetry, and the `(tokens intentionally omitted)` comment documents that tradeoff so future readers don't assume the field is broken.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nIf you were hoping for a different metric we don't have yet — e.g. turn count, session span, heatmap bucketing — that'd be a follow-up endpoint, not a change to `/me/recap`."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1412,"cache_read_input_tokens":140674,"output_tokens":1251,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1412,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":140674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1412},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKweVYPZi87hgWddRPNY","type":"assistant","uuid":"646f510b-9815-4048-aebf-f58201d07f2f","timestamp":"2026-04-23T02:50:46.479Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"kind-beaming-shannon"}
