{"parentUuid":"806a0356-f682-4ee1-85b5-f3abc52f56a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KepZzg8Danhhx65xkyMnae","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the full picture. Two separate mechanisms drive the two columns:\n\n| Column | Source | Why empty now |\n|---|---|---|\n| **me** (per-agent) | Per-checkpoint GET `/api/v1/cache/<repo>/checkpoints/<id>/analysis` | Your 92 local Claude Code checkpoint IDs don't match the 5 I seeded — each lookup returns 404 / incomplete → silently skipped |\n| **contributors** (per-agent) | New `/api/v1/me/recap` aggregate | Populated for 4 agents I seeded, empty for Codex (didn't seed it) |\n\n### Why me labels/skills/MCP/toolMix are blank\n\nThe me side enriches each local checkpoint by calling:\n\n```\nGET /api/v1/cache/entireio/cli/checkpoints/<checkpoint-id>/analysis\n```\n\nPer checkpoint. See `enrich.go:79-95`. It **needs a server-side analysis row keyed to that exact checkpoint_id**. My 5 seeded rows use checkpoint_ids like `f11ed66a2b62` (from the test-entire-local repo). Your local Claude Code sessions use different IDs — the 92 IDs in `.git/entire-sessions/*.json`. So every lookup is a miss.\n\nIn production this works fine because your local IDs match server IDs one-to-one (the CLI created them, the server analyzed them). In our local-dev seed, the IDs are disconnected.\n\n### Why Codex contributors is also blank\n\nI only seeded analyses for 4 agents (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Copilot CLI, OpenCode). No Codex rows in `repo_checkpoints` → Codex isn't in the `/me/recap` response → CLI renders `—`.\n\n### Quick fix if you want all agents fully lit\n\nEither:\n\n**A — seed Codex** so contributors column shows it too:\n\n```fish\ndocker exec api-mysql-1 mysql -u entire -pentire entire -e \"\nINSERT INTO repo_checkpoints (id, repo_id, checkpoint_id, agent, input_tokens, output_tokens, created_at, synced_at)\nVALUES (UUID(), '019d6918-9a35-7614-b00a-0a7124620260', 'codex-seed-1', 'Codex', 1200, 800, NOW(), NOW());\nINSERT INTO repo_checkpoint_analyses (id, repo_id, checkpoint_id, status, analysis_json, attempt_count, queued_at, started_at, completed_at)\nVALUES (UUID(), '019d6918-9a35-7614-b00a-0a7124620260', 'codex-seed-1', 'complete',\n  '{\\\"totalFilesChanged\\\":5,\\\"total_transcript_tokens\\\":3200,\\\"pipeline_version\\\":\\\"local-seed.v1\\\",\\\"extraction\\\":{\\\"labels\\\":[\\\"investigation\\\",\\\"refactor\\\"]},\\\"skillsUsed\\\":[\\\"codex:codex-rescue\\\"],\\\"mcpServersUsed\\\":[],\\\"toolProfile\\\":{\\\"categories\\\":{\\\"shell\\\":{\\\"count\\\":15},\\\"fileOps\\\":{\\\"count\\\":22},\\\"search\\\":{\\\"count\\\":9},\\\"mcp\\\":{\\\"count\\\":0},\\\"agent\\\":{\\\"count\\\":3},\\\"other\\\":{\\\"count\\\":1}},\\\"total\\\":50}}',\n  1, NOW(), NOW(), NOW());\n\"\n```\n\n**B — for me-side enrichment**, we'd have to seed analyses with your actual local checkpoint IDs (expensive — 92 of them for Claude Code alone). Not worth for this smoke test. In production this won't be an issue because your committed checkpoints really do have server analyses at their IDs.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThis is the architectural trade-off the `/me/recap` endpoint was designed around: contributors-side labels/skills need a server aggregate (one call, many checkpoints), while me-side labels come from per-checkpoint lookups that the CLI already caches. The endpoint intentionally doesn't replace the me-side per-checkpoint fetcher — doing so would either double-fetch every checkpoint or drop the cache granularity that makes the enrichment fast across sessions. The `me.*` fields in the response exist so web dashboards (no local cache) get a complete one-call picture; the CLI sticks with per-checkpoint because caching pays off there.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n**Bottom line**: the two empty-ish patterns you're seeing are local-dev artifacts, not endpoint bugs. In production your me column will populate (your IDs match the server's) and every agent you've used will have contributors data (full pipeline analysis runs for all of them).\n\nWant me to run the Codex seed so you see all 5 agents lit up in contributors, then draft the commit + PR?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":206316,"output_tokens":2593,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2593,"cache_read_input_tokens":206316,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKyNwB31hT2YXjuHMrN8","type":"assistant","uuid":"6900a978-48d1-4722-9318-41a359493ad9","timestamp":"2026-04-23T03:13:48.278Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"kind-beaming-shannon"}
