oceed with text-only brainstorming.\n\n**Per-question decision:** Even after the user accepts, decide FOR EACH QUESTION whether to use the browser or the terminal. The test: **would the user understand this better by seeing it than reading it?**\n\n- **Use the browser** for content that IS visual — mockups, wireframes, layout comparisons, architecture diagrams, side-by-side visual designs\n- **Use the terminal** for content that is text — requirements questions, conceptual choices, tradeoff lists, A/B/C/D text options, scope decisions\n\nA question about a UI topic is not automatically a visual question. \"What does personality mean in this context?\" is a conceptual question — use the terminal. \"Which wizard layout works better?\" is a visual question — use the browser.\n\nIf they agree to the companion, read the detailed guide before proceeding:\n`skills/brainstorming/visual-companion.md`\n\n\nARGUMENTS: Visual design pass for `entire recap` terminal output. We need to improve column formatting and overall visual elements.\n\n**Current state:** `entire recap` renders a 4-panel static/TUI output:\n1. Summary panel (top agent, top skill, focus, top model, totals)\n2. Activity strip (gradient bars for heatmap across the range)\n3. **Agents panel** (the main surface — per-agent cards with me/contributors columns, ~10 rows each: tokens, top labels, top skills, MCP servers, tool mix, sessions, checkpoints, distinct contribs, top models, top repos)\n4. Bottom panel (worktrees / labels / repos)\n\nCurrent agent-card column layout:\n```\nClaude Code\n                          me             contributors\n  Tokens                  2.9M           1k\n  Top labels              —            bug_fix 25%  feature_build 25%  refactor 25%\n  Top skills              —            code-simplifier, entire:session-handoff,\nsuperpowers:using-superpowers\n  MCP servers             —            linear-server\n  Tool mix                —            fileOps 61% · search 18% · shell 15%\n  Sessions                15             2\n  Checkpoints             92             2\n  Distinct contribs       —            1\n  Top models              claude-opus-4-7[1m], claude-opus-4-6[1m] —\n  Top repos               entireio/cli (15) —\n```\n\n**Pain points the user has flagged this session:**\n- Column alignment feels off — me and contributors values sometimes wrap awkwardly (top skills line wrapping mid-value, top models trailing `—` dangling)\n- Empty cells (`—`) are load-bearing for consistent card height but visually heavy\n- Long comma-separated lists (top skills, top models) blow out the column width\n- No visual hierarchy between deterministic rows (sessions/checkpoints, always populated) and LLM-dependent rows (labels/skills, often empty when analyses haven't run)\n- Header row \"me | contributors\" sits at per-agent card level, duplicates across every card\n- User wants the command to feel polished — it's the read-only surface most people will see daily\n\n**Constraints:**\n- Terminal width: assume 100-120 cols as the common case, gracefully degrade at 80\n- Uses lipgloss for styling, bubbletea for TUI mode, plain ANSI-free text when piped\n- Palette already defined: amber 214 (accent), violet 99 (modes), teal 36 (focus), green 43 (activity), magenta 170 (agents), 256-color base — semantic label colors per label (feature_build=42, bug_fix=203, etc.)\n- Must work in `NO_COLOR=1` (Unicode geometry only, no color)\n- Must work in `ACCESSIBLE=1` (no box-drawing, linear sections)\n- Reuse existing primitives: `render_chart.go` (gradient bars), `render_panel.go` (rounded borders), 256-color semantic label map\n\n**Goals for the redesign:**\n- Stronger visual hierarchy so the eye goes to the signal (active agent with lots of data) not the placeholders\n- Tighter column layout — no awkward mid-value wraps\n- Better treatment of empty rows (should they collapse? be muted? be grouped?)\n- Consider consolidating me/contributors into something other than side-by-side columns if a better visual exists (e.g. inline delta, overlay bars, grouped rows)\n- Keep the command feeling at home with `entire status` / `entire search` / other CLI surfaces in this repo\n\nGoal: produce a spec we can hand off to a plan or directly implement."}]},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"e138c7a0-d225-4dcd-baa1-cac80b2efd80","timestamp":"2026-04-23T03:23:18.242Z","sourceToolUseID":"toolu_01D6Yw6V2W3hQ2LH4VVsfUcH","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"kind-beaming-shannon"}
