lass=\"team-label\">team labels</span>    <span class=\"red\">● bug_fix</span>  <span class=\"green\">● feature_build</span>  <span class=\"yellow\">● refactor</span>              <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"team-label\">team skills</span>    <span class=\"cyan\">code-simplifier</span>, <span class=\"cyan\">session-handoff</span>, <span class=\"cyan\">using-super…</span>     <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"team-label\">team tool mix</span>  fileOps 61% · search 18% · shell 15%                      <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>                                                                           <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"you-label\">your models</span>    claude-opus-4-7[1m], claude-opus-4-6[1m]                   <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"you-label\">your repos</span>     entireio/cli (15)                                          <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯</span></pre></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"note\">Full card. 3 comparison bars + 3 team rows + 2 your rows = 9 content rows total. Labels use the semantic color palette you already have (red for bug_fix, green for feature_build, etc.).</div>\n\n<div class=\"mockup\">\n  <div class=\"mockup-header\">Scenario 2 — Only you have data (Codex, no team analyses)</div>\n  <div class=\"mockup-body\"><pre>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span> <span class=\"amber\">Codex</span>                                                                     <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   tokens       <span class=\"you-bar\">█████████████████████████████████████</span>      <span class=\"value\">647k / —</span>          <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   sessions     <span class=\"you-bar\">█████████████████████████████████████</span>      <span class=\"value\">24 / —</span>            <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>                                                                           <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"you-label\">your models</span>    gpt-5.4                                                    <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"you-label\">your repos</span>     entireio/cli (24)                                          <span class=\"label\">│</span></pre></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"note\">Checkpoints row is <strong>dropped entirely</strong> because both sides are 0. Team-qualitative rows (labels, skills, tool mix) <strong>don't appear</strong> because team has no data. No dangling <code>—</code> anywhere.</div>\n\n<div class=\"mockup\">\n  <div class=\"mockup-header\">Scenario 3 — Team &gt; you (Gemini CLI; team dominates)</div>\n  <div class=\"mockup-body\"><pre>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span> <span class=\"amber\">Gemini CLI</span>                                                                <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   tokens       <span class=\"you-bar\">██</span><span class=\"team-bar\">▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒</span>  <span class=\"value\">1k / 14k</span>            <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   checkpoints  <span class=\"you-bar\">█</span><span class=\"team-bar\">▒</span>                                  <span class=\"value\">0 / 1</span>              <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>                                                                           <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"team-label\">team labels</span>    <span class=\"cyan\">● investigation</span>  <span class=\"green\">● documentation</span>                        <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"team-label\">team skills</span>    <span class=\"cyan\">entire:session-handoff</span>                                   <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"team-label\">team tool mix</span>  search 56% · fileOps 32% · shell 7%                       <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>                                                                           <span class=\"label\">│</span>\n<span class=\"label\">│</span>   <span class=\"you-label\">your repos</span>     entireio/cli (1)                                           <span class=\"label\">│</span></pre></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"note\">Bar flips: team's share is the longer pattern, you is the small lead segment. <code>sessions</code> row is dropped (you = 0, team = 0 for sessions here). <code>your models</code> is dropped (no model data on this session). The card shrinks to what's actually meaningful.</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"color:#eee; margin-top: 28px;\">Rules captured in this card</h3>\n<ul style=\"color:#ccc;\">\n  <li><strong>Panel header once:</strong> <code>you ███ team ▒</code> appears at top of Agents panel, not per card.</li>\n  <li><strong>Bar scaling:</strong> proportional to <code>max(you, team)</code>. Whichever side is larger fills; the smaller overlays in dot pattern.</li>\n  <li><strong>Zero-both rows drop:</strong> no \"sessions 0 / 0\" rows.</li>\n  <li><strong>Group 1 — bars:</strong> tokens, sessions, checkpoints. Quantitative comparisons.</li>\n  <li><strong>Group 2 — team qualitative:</strong> labels, skills, tool mix. Only shown when team has data.</li>\n  <li><strong>Group 3 — your qualitative:</strong> models, repos. Only shown when you have data.</li>\n  <li><strong>Numeric readout:</strong> always <code>you / team</code>, with <code>—</code> placeholder only in the readout (never on its own row).