e (`green-0` / `237`). Today's default only renders cells where activity exists, which makes ranges look broken.\n- **Pad to full terminal width** so axis labels align under their cells.\n- **Rightmost cell is always today**, leftmost is range start. Fixed anchoring.\n- **Peak annotation** — `most active: <date>` top-right of the strip. Renders only when at least one day has non-zero activity. The peak is the day with max `you_sessions + team_sessions`.\n- Intra-day (`--day`) and 7-day (`--week`) variants reuse the existing `renderIntraDayStrip` / day-of-week-initials label row in `render_static.go` — same padding rules apply there.\n\n## Agents panel spec\n\nThe Agents panel header carries the comparison legend, so per-card headers are gone:\n\n```\n╭─ Agents · last 90 days ────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                                                you ███   team ▒            │\n│                                                                            │\n│ <agent cards here, separated by blank lines>                               │\n│                                                                            │\n╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n```\n\n**Panel rules:**\n- Title includes the range: `Agents · last 90 days`.\n- Legend row appears once under the title when view is `both`. In `you` or `team` single views, the legend is omitted (the bar color tells you which side).\n- Cards sorted by combined `you_sessions + team_sessions` descending.\n- No pagination — show every agent with any data. Typical case is 2–6 agents.\n- Empty panel: single line `(no agent activity in range)`, muted.\n\n### Per-agent card (view: both)\n\n```\nClaude Code\n  tokens       █████████████████████████████████▒  2.9M / 1k\n  sessions     █████████████████████▒▒▒             15 / 2\n  checkpoints  ██████████████████████████████▒      92 / 2\n\n  team labels    ● bug_fix  ● feature_build  ● refactor\n  team skills    code-simplifier, session-handoff, using-super…\n  team tool mix  fileOps 61% · search 18% · shell 15%\n\n  your models    claude-opus-4-7[1m], claude-opus-4-6[1m]\n  your repos     entireio/cli (15)\n```\n\n**Card structure — three field groups in fixed order, separated by blank lines:**\n\n1. **Comparison bars** — `tokens`, `sessions`, `checkpoints`.\n   - Each row: label + bar + readout.\n   - Bar total width is panel-relative (budget roughly half the panel's inner width).\n   - Bar fill: the larger side fills proportionally to `max(you, team)`. The smaller side overlays as dot pattern (`▒`) extending to its proportional length.\n   - If `you >= team`: amber fill up to `you_ratio × width`, then magenta dots up to `team_ratio × width`.\n   - If `team > you`: flipped — magenta fill up to `team_ratio × width`, amber fill up to `you_ratio × width`.\n   - Readout: `<you_value> / <team_value>`, human-formatted (`2.9M / 1k`, not `2901234 / 1045`). Use `formatTokens` for tokens; integers verbatim for sessions/checkpoints.\n   - If a row has both sides zero, the **row drops entirely**. No `0 / 0` clutter.\n   - If one side is nil (not zero — genuinely absent because the user isn't logged in or data hasn't synced), that side shows `—` in the readout but the bar renders as whatever data exists.\n2. **Team qualitative fields** — `team labels`, `team skills`, `team tool mix`.\n   - Prefixed `team` (magenta-bold label) when view is `both` to disambiguate source.\n   - In view `team`, the prefix drops; the column header is implied.\n   - In view `you`, this entire block is skipped (team fields have no you equivalent).\n   - Block skipped when team has no analysis data.\n   - Labels render with semantic per-label colors (existing palette in `styles.go`). Skills render in cyan. Tool mix renders plain.\n   - Soft-truncate with `…` when the single-line content exceeds the inner panel width. Never wrap.\n3. **Your qualitative fields** — `your models`, `your repos`.\n   - Prefixed `your` (amber-bold label) when view is `both`.\n   - In view `you`, prefix drops.\n   - In view `team`, this entire block is skipped.\n   - Block skipped when you have no local session data for this agent.\n\n### Empty-row behavior (consolidated)\n\nNo `—` placeholder rows. The old design kept card shape consistent with `—` in every missing slot. The new design **drops rows** instead. Cards naturally expand or shrink to what's actually meaningful.\n\nThe only `—` that ever renders is **inside the readout** of a comparison bar, e.g. `647k / —`, when one side has a value and the other is nil. This is a single-glyph marker in a row that's already present for a reason.\n\n### View toggle semantics\n\n| Aspect | view: you | view: team | view: both (default) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bar color | amber fill only | magenta fill only | amber fill + magenta overlay |\n| Bar scale | max of you values across agents | max of team values across agents | max(you, team) per row |\n| Numeric readout | `<you>` | `<team>` | `<you> / <team>` |\n| Qualitative rows | models, repos (no prefix) | labels, skills, tool mix (no prefix) | both groups with `your` / `team` prefix |\n| Legend row | hidden | hidden | shown |\n| Total card width | narrow (one column's worth) | narrow | wide |\n\nKeyboard/flag:\n- TUI: `v` cycles `you → team → both`.\n- Static: `--view me|contributors|both` (flag names stay as-is for continuity with existing contract).\n\n## Empty-state handling\n\n- **No data at all in range** — panel renders with empty body lines. Summary shows `you  0 sessions  0 checkpoints  0 tok` + `team 0 …`. Activity strip renders the full cell grid at the zero shade. Agents panel shows `(no agent activity in range)`. No diagnostic note.\n- **Not logged in** — me side renders from local data; team side shows `—` in readouts; legend/prefixes still explain the split. Diagnostic note at the footer: `ℹ Sign in with \"entire login\" to see team comparisons.`\n- **Labels still analyzing** — me side may be fully empty for labels/skills/tool mix (analyses in-flight). Team side may be full. Diagnostic note at the footer: `ℹ Labels require server analysis (may take a few minutes after committing).` Note renders only when at least one agent card has a team block but no me label data.\n\n## Color & accessibility rules\n\n- **Palette** — reuse existing `styles.go` constants. New additions: no colors added. `you` uses `colorAccent` (amber 214). `team` uses a new style `styles.team` bound to a magenta (say color `170`, matches the existing agents-panel magenta noted in earlier design docs).\n- **`NO_COLOR=1`** — all amber/magenta/semantic styles become no-ops. The bars still render (they're Unicode geometry, not color-dependent). Prefixes still read correctly because they're plain text (`you`, `team`, `your`). Dot-pattern overlay `▒` is still visible against fill `█`. The view remains scannable without any color.\n- **`ACCESSIBLE=1`** — drop box-drawing. Panels become `## Summary`, `## Activity`, `## Agents` sections with blank-line separators. Comparison bars degrade to `you: 2.9M / team: 1k` plain text lines — the bar glyph is skipped (screen readers would announce every cell). Everything else collapses to indented lists under the section headers.\n\n## Concrete code changes\n\nThe spec maps to these file touches. An implementation plan will break these into ordered steps:\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/recap.go` — remove `--30` flag and `f.d30` field.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go` — remove `Range30d` from the `RangeKey` enum (or keep the constant and map it to `RangeMonth` if any persisted state references it).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static.go`\n  - `renderHeader`: drop the `30d` tab option.\n  - `renderSummaryBand`: rewrite to the new `you / team / top / context` shape.\n  - `renderActivityStrip`: pad to full width, always render zero cells, annotate peak.\n  - `renderBottomPanel`: delete (or inline a no-op). The entire bottom-panel code path is removed.\n  - `RenderStatic`: drop the bottom-panel write.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/recap/agents_card.go`\n  - Rewrite the per-card renderer around the three-group structure.\n  - Add a `renderComparisonBar` helper (me/team bar with overlay, proportional fill, readout).\n  - Remove the `MCP servers` row, the `Distinct contribs` row.\n  - Panel-level legend row emitted once per call, not per card.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/recap/styles.go` — add `team lipgloss.Style` (magenta bold). Possibly add a helper `styles.prefixYou()` / `styles.prefixTeam()` to keep renderer call sites short.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go` — add `v` keybinding for view cycling. Update help text.\n\n## Out of scope for v1\n\nThese are called out so reviewers don't ask \"why isn't X in the spec\":\n\n- No drill-down overlay on an agent card. Enter-on-agent-row was part of the old design; keep postponed.\n- No session list panel. Sessions surface in `entire sessions` today, no duplication needed.\n- No per-day breakdown drill-down on the activity strip. Date ranges stay visual-only.\n- Comparison bars are proportional within their own row, not normalized across all rows. Cross-row comparison isn't a stated goal.\n- No unit tests for `renderComparisonBar` specifically in this spec — the plan will specify TDD for it.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"26e8a3f2-6830-4ba5-9619-cb32b3de029f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"b35707d3-641d-4b8a-83b2-52ef9ab92ecf","version":"2.1.116","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"kind-beaming-shannon"}
