{"parentUuid":"d108d446-a968-4f54-a69a-47612379a6bb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016uYFi44DctTksbnyek7saL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VzfCchdbwtampccFsjGYLC","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/2026-04-22-entire-recap-visual-redesign-design.md","old_string":"1. **Comparison bars** — `tokens`, `sessions`, `checkpoints`.\n   - Each row: label + bar + readout.\n   - Bar total width is panel-relative (budget roughly half the panel's inner width).\n   - Bar fill: the larger side fills proportionally to `max(you, team)`. The smaller side overlays as dot pattern (`▒`) extending to its proportional length.\n   - If `you >= team`: amber fill up to `you_ratio × width`, then magenta dots up to `team_ratio × width`.\n   - If `team > you`: flipped — magenta fill up to `team_ratio × width`, amber fill up to `you_ratio × width`.\n   - Readout: `<you_value> / <team_value>`, human-formatted (`2.9M / 1k`, not `2901234 / 1045`). Use `formatTokens` for tokens; integers verbatim for sessions/checkpoints.\n   - If a row has both sides zero, the **row drops entirely**. No `0 / 0` clutter.\n   - If one side is nil (not zero — genuinely absent because the user isn't logged in or data hasn't synced), that side shows `—` in the readout but the bar renders as whatever data exists.","new_string":"1. **Comparison bars** — `tokens`, `sessions`, `checkpoints`.\n   - Each row: label + bar + readout.\n   - **Bar width formula**: `barWidth = innerPanelWidth - labelWidth - readoutWidth - 4` (4 = left indent + two padding gaps). `labelWidth = 12` (longest label \"checkpoints\" + padding). `readoutWidth = 14` (accommodates \"2.9M / 999k\").\n   - **Minimum bar width**: 12 cells. Below that, the bar is dropped and the readout is rendered alone on the row (e.g. `tokens  2.9M / 1k`). This only matters below ~70 col terminals.\n   - **Maximum bar width**: 40 cells, so even wide terminals don't stretch the bar past the visual sweet spot.\n   - Bar fill: the larger side fills proportionally to `max(you, team)`. The smaller side overlays as dot pattern (`▒`) extending to its proportional length.\n     - If `you > team`: amber fill `█` for `⌈you_ratio × width⌉` cells, magenta dots `▒` for `⌈team_ratio × width⌉` cells (overlaying the first N cells of the amber fill).\n     - If `team > you`: flipped — magenta fill `█` for the team portion, amber fill `█` for the you portion at the start (shorter).\n     - If `you == team` (both non-zero): amber fill full width; magenta dots overlay full width too. They alternate by priority (magenta wins on even columns, amber on odd) to make equality visible as a striped bar.\n   - **Rounding**: any non-zero value gets a minimum of **1 cell** after rounding. Only `0` renders as empty cells in that region. This prevents tiny values (e.g. 1 session vs 1000) from visually disappearing.\n   - Readout: `<you_value> / <team_value>`, human-formatted (`2.9M / 1k`, not `2901234 / 1045`). Use `formatTokens` for tokens; integers verbatim for sessions/checkpoints.\n   - If a row has both sides zero, the **row drops entirely**. No `0 / 0` clutter.\n   - If one side is nil (not zero — genuinely absent because the user isn't logged in or data hasn't synced), that side shows `—` in the readout but the bar renders as whatever data exists."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_read_input_tokens":325870,"output_tokens":1397,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":325870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cach