ap.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/contributors.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/load.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/enrich.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/cache.go\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 0b: Verify typecheck + tests still pass before committing**\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test\n```\n\nExpected: all green. If red, fix before proceeding.\n\n- [ ] **Step 0c: Commit the pairing**\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap): wire CLI to /api/v1/me/recap endpoint\n\nPairs with entirehq/entire.io#1604. Prefers the consolidated /me/recap\nendpoint when available; falls back to the three-endpoint stack when\nthe server doesn't have /me/recap yet.\n\nAdds stampRepos so cp.Repo is populated for local checkpoints, adds\nhasUsefulSignal to invalidate cache entries with empty payloads, and\nadds the AnalysisStatusComplete guard in EnrichCheckpoint.\n\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 0d: Reset the rendering files so this plan starts from a clean baseline**\n\nThe visual-redesign files (`agents_card.go`, `render_static.go`, `tui.go`, `styles.go`, and their tests) have uncommitted experimental edits from prior work. Reset them so the plan's TDD steps aren't fighting prior state:\n\n```bash\ngit checkout -- cmd/entire/cli/recap/agents_card.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/agents_card_test.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static_test.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui_test.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/api_types.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/recap_view.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go cmd/entire/cli/recap_test.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/contributors_test.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/enrich_test.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/cache_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 0e: Verify clean baseline**\n\n```bash\ngit status --short cmd/entire/cli/recap/ cmd/entire/cli/recap.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/\n```\n\nExpected: only `me_recap.go` should be untracked (or freshly committed); everything else should be clean.\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n| File | Purpose | Change type |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar.go` | `renderComparisonBar` primitive — the new bar renderer | **Create** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar_test.go` | 9 unit tests from the spec's testing section | **Create** |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go` | `RangeKey` enum; remove `Range30d` | Modify |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap.go` | Cobra command; remove `--30` flag | Modify |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/styles.go` | Add `team` style + `prefixYou` / `prefixTeam` helpers | Modify |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static.go` | Rewrite `renderSummaryBand`, `renderActivityStrip`, `renderHeader`; delete `renderBottomPanel`; simplify `RenderStatic` | Modify |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static_test.go` | Update assertions for new summary/activity shape; drop bottom-panel tests | Modify |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/agents_card.go` | Rewrite per-agent card around three field groups + view toggle | Modify (rewrite) |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/agents_card_test.go` | Rewrite to match new card shape, add view-toggle cases | Modify |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go` | Add `v` keybinding for view cycling; update help text | Modify |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui_test.go` | Add view-cycle test | Modify |\n\nEach file has one clear responsibility. `render_bar.go` is new because the bar primitive is complex enough (stripes, overlay, rounding rules) to deserve isolation — it will be reusable by future panels too.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Flag + enum cleanup\n\nSmall, low-risk, green-the-whole-way. Removes `--30` and `Range30d`.\n\n### Task 1: Remove `Range30d` from the enum\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/model_test.go` (if exists; otherwise skip)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Find current enum definition**\n\n```bash\ngrep -nE 'Range30d|RangeKey' cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write a failing test asserting `Range30d` does not exist**\n\nCreate `cmd/entire/cli/recap/model_range_test.go` with:\n\n```go\npackage recap\n\nimport \"testing\"\n\nfunc TestRangeKey_Range30dRemoved(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // Compile-time check: if Range30d exists, this file won't compile.\n    // The test body asserts the enum has exactly the expected members.\n    want := []RangeKey{RangeDay, RangeWeek, RangeMonth, Range90d}\n    if len(want) != 4 {\n        t.Fatalf(\"expected 4 range keys, got %d\", len(want))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run — expect compile failure because `Range30d` is still referenced elsewhere**\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/ -run TestRangeKey_Range30dRemoved -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: compile error pointing at every remaining `Range30d` reference.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Delete `Range30d` from the enum + its `String()`/`Bounds()` cases**\n\nIn `model.go`, remove `Range30d` from the const block, the `String()` switch, and the `Bounds()` switch. Remove any related comment.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Fix every remaining reference**\n\n```bash\ngrep -rn 'Range30d' cmd/entire/cli/recap/ cmd/entire/cli/\n```\n\nFor each hit: delete the case or change it to `RangeMonth` (cache-key mapping is fine to drop since the feature hasn't shipped per the spec).\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run tests — expect green**\n\n```bash\nmise run test 2>&1 | tail -20\n```\n\nExpected: all tests pass.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit**\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/model_range_test.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(recap): remove Range30d from RangeKey enum\n\n--30 is being removed in favor of --month (spec 2026-04-22).\nRange30d has no persisted state so no migration needed.\n\"\n```\n\n### Task 2: Remove `--30` flag + `30d` header tab\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static.go` (renderHeader)\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap_test.go` if it asserts on `--30`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Locate the flag and the header tab**\n\n```bash\ngrep -nE '\"30\"|--30|30d|d30' cmd/entire/cli/recap.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static.go\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write a failing test asserting the header doesn't contain `30d`**\n\nAdd to `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static_test.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestRenderHeader_No30dTab(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    v := View{Range: Range90d, Mode: ViewBoth}\n    out := renderHeader(v, \"\", NewStyles(false))\n    if strings.Contains(out, \"30d\") {\n        t.Errorf(\"header should not contain 30d tab; got %q\", out)\n    }\n    if strings.Contains(out, \"30\") && !strings.Contains(out, \"90d\") {\n        // Be lenient: 90d is fine, 30d alone is not.\n        t.Errorf(\"header contains stray 30 outside 90d; got %q\", out)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run — expect failure**\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/ -run TestRenderHeader_No30dTab -count=1 -v\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Remove the `30d` tab from `renderHeader`'s `rangeLabels` slice**\n\nIn `render_static.go`, find the `rangeLabels` slice and delete the `{\"30d\", Range30d}` entry.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Remove `--30` flag from `recap.go`**\n\nRemove the `BoolVar(&f.d30, \"30\", ...)` line and the `d30` field on the flags struct. Remove any code that checks `f.d30` (there should be a mapping from flags → `RangeKey`; delete the `case f.d30: return Range30d` branch).\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run tests — expect green**\n\n```bash\nmise run test 2>&1 | tail -20\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Manual smoke — verify cobra rejects `--30`**\n\n```bash\ngo run ./cmd/entire recap --30 2>&1 | head -3\n```\n\nExpected: `Error: unknown flag: --30` with a cobra suggestion (likely `--90`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Commit**\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/recap.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static_test.go\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap): remove --30 flag (redundant with --month)\n\nSpec: docs/2026-04-22-entire-recap-visual-redesign-design.md\nUsers who type --30 get cobra's native unknown-flag error with\nsuggestion pointing at --90 or --month.\n\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 2: Styles + `renderComparisonBar` primitive\n\nTDD-heavy. The bar is the most complex new primitive; the 9 unit tests from the spec drive the implementation.\n\n### Task 3: Add `team` style + prefix helpers\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/styles.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/styles_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing test**\n\nAdd to `styles_test.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestStyles_Team(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    s := NewStyles(true)\n    out := s.team.Render(\"team\")\n    if !strings.Contains(out, \"team\") {\n        t.Errorf(\"team style should render 'team'; got %q\", out)\n    }\n    // When color is off, team should be a no-op.\n    sOff := NewStyles(false)\n    if got := sOff.team.Render(\"team\"); got != \"team\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"team style (color off) should be plain text; got %q\", got)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run — expect failure (field doesn't exist)**\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/ -run TestStyles_Team -count=1 -v\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add the field + constructor wiring**\n\nIn `styles.go`:\n\n```go\n// Add to color constants block:\nconst colorTeam = \"170\" // magenta — team/contributors side accent\n\n// Add to Styles struct:\nteam lipgloss.Style\n\n// Add to NewStyles() when useColor is true:\nteam: lipgloss.NewStyle().Foreground(lipgloss.Color(colorTeam)).Bold(true),\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run — expect green**\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/ -run TestStyles_Team -count=1 -v\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/recap/styles.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/styles_test.go\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap): add team style for magenta contributors accent\"\n```\n\n### Task 4: Create `renderComparisonBar` with the 9 spec tests\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Create the test file with all 9 cases (failing)**\n\nWrite `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar_test.go`:\n\n```go\npackage recap\n\nimport (\n    \"strings\"\n    \"testing\"\n)\n\n// Helpers --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n// countRunes counts how many of the given runes appear in s (after stripping\n// ANSI). Used to assert bar-cell counts without coupling to exact styling.\nfunc countRunes(s string, r rune) int {\n    // Render tests use NewStyles(false) so ANSI escapes are absent — plain\n    // rune count is accurate.\n    n := 0\n    for _, c := range s {\n        if c == r {\n            n++\n        }\n    }\n    return n\n}\n\n// Test cases from spec §Testing strategy ------------------------------------\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_YouGreater(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // you=100, team=25, width=20 → you fills 20, team overlays 5.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(100, 25, 20, NewStyles(false))\n    if n := countRunes(got, '█'); n != 15 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 15 amber █ cells (20 - 5 team overlay); got %d in %q\", n, got)\n    }\n    if n := countRunes(got, '▒'); n != 5 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 5 magenta ▒ cells; got %d in %q\", n, got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_TeamGreater(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // you=25, team=100, width=20 → team fills 20 (█), you fills 5 at start.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(25, 100, 20, NewStyles(false))\n    // With no color, both sides render as █, so assert total fill not color.\n    if n := countRunes(got, '█'); n != 20 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 20 fill cells total; got %d in %q\", n, got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_Equal(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // you=50, team=50, width=10 → striped (magenta on even, amber on odd)\n    got := renderComparisonBar(50, 50, 10, NewStyles(false))\n    amberCount := countRunes(got, '█')\n    dotCount := countRunes(got, '▒')\n    if amberCount != 5 || dotCount != 5 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 5 █ + 5 ▒ striped; got amber=%d dot=%d in %q\", amberCount, dotCount, got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_YouOnly(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // you=100, team=0 → full amber, no overlay.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(100, 0, 20, NewStyles(false))\n    if n := countRunes(got, '█'); n != 20 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 20 █ cells; got %d in %q\", n, got)\n    }\n    if n := countRunes(got, '▒'); n != 0 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 0 ▒ cells; got %d in %q\", n, got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_TeamOnly(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // you=0, team=100 → full magenta, no overlay.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(0, 100, 20, NewStyles(false))\n    if n := countRunes(got, '█'); n != 20 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 20 █ cells (team fill); got %d in %q\", n, got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_BothZero(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // Both zero → empty string; caller drops the row.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(0, 0, 20, NewStyles(false))\n    if got != \"\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected empty bar when both zero; got %q\", got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_TinyYouHugeTeam(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // you=1, team=1000, width=20 → you gets 1 cell (minimum), team fills 20.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(1, 1000, 20, NewStyles(false))\n    if countRunes(got, '█') < 1 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected at least 1 cell for tiny you value; got %q\", got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_NarrowClampsToMin(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // width=8 requested, but min is 12. Bar should return \"\" so caller\n    // falls back to readout-only mode.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(100, 50, 8, NewStyles(false))\n    if got != \"\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected empty when width < 12; got %q\", got)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderComparisonBar_WideClampsToMax(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    // width=200 requested, but max is 40.\n    got := renderComparisonBar(100, 100, 200, NewStyles(false))\n    total := countRunes(got, '█') + countRunes(got, '▒')\n    if total != 40 {\n        t.Errorf(\"expected 40 total cells when clamped; got %d in %q\", total, got)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run — expect 9 failures (function doesn't exist)**\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/ -run TestRenderComparisonBar -count=1 -v\n```\n\nExpected: `undefined: renderComparisonBar` compile error.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement `renderComparisonBar`**\n\nCreate `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar.go`:\n\n```go\npackage recap\n\nimport \"strings\"\n\nconst (\n    barMinWidth = 12\n    barMaxWidth = 40\n)\n\n// renderComparisonBar renders a single horizontal bar comparing `you` vs\n// `team` values. Rules (from spec §Agents panel spec):\n//   - Both zero: returns \"\" so the caller drops the row entirely.\n//   - you > team: amber █ fills width; magenta ▒ overlays the first\n//     `team_ratio × width` cells.\n//   - team > you: flipped — magenta █ fills width; amber █ fills the\n//     first `you_ratio × width` cells (no ▒ overlay).\n//   - you == team (both non-zero): striped — magenta ▒ on even columns,\n//     amber █ on odd columns.\n//   - Non-zero values always render at least 1 cell to stay visible.\n//   - width clamped to [barMinWidth, barMaxWidth]. If requested width is\n//     below the minimum, returns \"\" so the caller renders readout-only.\nfunc renderComparisonBar(you, team, width int, styles Styles) string {\n    if you == 0 && team == 0 {\n        return \"\"\n    }\n    if width < barMinWidth {\n        return \"\"\n    }\n    if width > barMaxWidth {\n        width = barMaxWidth\n    }\n\n    // Equal-value striped case.\n    if you == team && you > 0 {\n        var b strings.Builder\n        for i := 0; i < width; i++ {\n            if i%2 == 0 {\n                b.WriteString(styles.team.Render(\"▒\"))\n            } else {\n                b.WriteString(styles.accent.Render(\"█\"))\n            }\n        }\n        return b.String()\n    }\n\n    // you-dominant: amber fill width, team dot-overlay.\n    if you > team {\n        teamCells := cellsFor(team, you, width)\n        youCells := width - teamCells\n        if team > 0 && teamCells == 0 {\n            teamCells = 1\n            youCells = width - 1\n        }\n        return strings.Repeat(styles.accent.Render(\"█\"), youCells) +\n            strings.Repeat(styles.team.Render(\"▒\"), teamCells)\n    }\n\n    // team-dominant: magenta fill width, amber fills start.\n    teamTotal := width\n    youCells := cellsFor(you, team, width)\n    if you > 0 && youCells == 0 {\n        youCells = 1\n    }\n    teamCells := teamTotal - youCells\n    return strings.Repeat(styles.accent.Render(\"█\"), youCells) +\n        strings.Repeat(styles.team.Render(\"█\"), teamCells)\n}\n\n// cellsFor returns the number of cells that should represent `value` when\n// the total bar is `width` and the larger side is `max`. Rounds to the\n// nearest integer; always returns at least 1 for non-zero values (the\n// minimum-1-cell rule from the spec).\nfunc cellsFor(value, max, width int) int {\n    if max == 0 {\n        return 0\n    }\n    n := (value*width + max/2) / max // rounded integer division\n    if value > 0 && n == 0 {\n        return 1\n    }\n    if n > width {\n        return width\n    }\n    return n\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests — expect 9 passes**\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/ -run TestRenderComparisonBar -count=1 -v\n```\n\nExpected: `--- PASS` for all 9. If any fail, iterate on the implementation (the test outputs will point at the specific scenario).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run the full package suite**\n\n```bash\nmise run test 2>&1 | tail -10\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Commit**\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar_test.go\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap): add renderComparisonBar primitive (TDD)\n\n9 unit tests cover every case from spec §Testing strategy:\nyou>team, team>you, equal, one-sided, tiny-vs-huge, narrow/wide\nwidth clamping, both-zero drop.\n\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 3: Summary panel rewrite\n\nRebuilds `renderSummaryBand` around the new you/team/top/context structure.\n\n### Task 5: Rewrite summary band\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_static_test.go`\n- Possibly modify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go` if `SummaryBand` struct needs fields\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Inspect the `SummaryBand` struct to confirm fields available**\n\n```bash\ngrep -nE 'type SummaryBand|Summary\\s+\\w' cmd/entire/cli/recap/model.go\n```\n\nIf missing fields like `YouSessions`, `YouCheckpoints`, `YouTokens`, `TeamSessions`, `TeamCheckpoints`, `TeamTokens`, `TopAgent`, `TopSkill`, `TopLabel`, `TopModel`, `AgentCount`, `RepoCount`, `ActiveDays` — add them to the struct.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing tests for the new shape**\n\nReplace existing `TestRenderSummaryBand*` tests in `render_static_test.go` with:\n\n```go\nfunc TestRenderSummaryBand_AllTopSignals(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    s := SummaryBand{\n        RangeLabel: \"Last 90 days\",\n        YouSessions: 40, YouCheckpoints: 92, YouTokens: 3_500_000,\n        TeamSessions: 5, TeamCheckpoints: 6, TeamTokens: 17_000,\n        TopAgent: \"Codex\", TopSkill: \"code-simplifier\",\n        TopLabel: \"bug_fix\", TopModel: \"claude-opus-4-7[1m]\",\n        AgentCount: 5, RepoCount: 1, ActiveDays: 14,\n    }\n    got := renderSummaryBand(s, NewStyles(false))\n    for _, want := range []string{\n        \"Last 90 days\",\n        \"you\", \"40 sessions\", \"92 checkpoints\", \"3.5M tok\",\n        \"team\", \"5 sessions\", \"6 checkpoints\", \"17k tok\",\n        \"top\", \"Codex\", \"code-simplifier\", \"bug_fix\", \"claude-opus-4-7[1m]\",\n        \"5 agents\", \"1 repo\", \"14 