 width tiers and narrow-terminal behavior that Chunk 8 addresses, but hard-coding 96 means the `innerWidth` param to `renderAgentCard` is unused at runtime — the card ignores the passed width. Chunk 8's narrow-width test passes `36` directly and works because it threads through `innerWidth` param into `renderBarRows`. Inconsistency: `renderAgentsView` calls `renderAgentCard(c, mode, panelInnerWidth(), styles)` ignoring actual terminal width. This will break responsive behavior.\n\n- **Chunk 5, Task 7, Step 3**: Helpers `formatLabelList`, `formatList`, `formatToolMix`, `formatRepoList`, `formatTokens` are referenced but not defined. Plan says \"may already exist or need creating\" — this is hand-wavy; the plan should require verification before Step 4 runs.\n\n- **Chunk 7, Task 9, Step 2**: Test uses `newModel(View{Mode: ViewBoth})` and `Model` types without confirming these names in the existing code. Plan acknowledges \"Adjust `newModel` / `Model` to match the actual type names\" — minor hand-wave, but acceptable since a prior Step (Step 1 grep) is meant to discover them.\n\n- **Chunk 5, agents_card_test.go**: Missing a test for `ViewContributors` mode on `renderAgentCard` (you-only and both-view are covered, team-only is not). Spec has a team-only view toggle — gap in coverage.\n\n- **File size**: `render_static.go` after Chunks 3/4/6 will carry summary band rewrite, activity strip rewrite, header rewrite, range helpers, label-style helper, and `RenderStatic` orchestrator. Likely >400 lines and growing. Consider splitting `renderSummaryBand` and its helpers into a `render_summary.go`.\n\n**Recommendations (advisory):**\n\n- Split `render_static.go` into `render_summary.go`, `render_activity.go`, and keep `render_static.go` as the composition shell.\n- Add an explicit step at the top of Chunk 5 to enumerate which format helpers (`formatTokens`, `formatList`, `formatLabelList`, `formatToolMix`, `formatRepoList`) already exist via `grep`, then list any that need creation as sub-steps.\n- In Chunk 5, replace the `panelInnerWidth()` hardcoded 96 with a threaded `terminalWidth` parameter from `RenderStatic`, so Chunk 8's narrow-width handling is consistent with everyday rendering.\n- Add a `ViewContributors` unit test for `renderAgentCard` to ensure all three view modes have coverage symmetry.\n- Consider adding a snapshot/golden-file test for `RenderStatic` at the end of Chunk 6 that pins the full page shape — this catches regressions cheaply.\n\nOverall: The plan is detailed, TDD-disciplined, and executable. The 9 spec-required `renderComparisonBar` cases are all present. The issues above are mostly minor hand-waves around helper function existence and one architectural quibble (hardcoded width); none block a skilled Go developer from executing chunk-by-chunk."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a214de72c72a8ab56 (use SendMessage with to: 'a214de72c72a8ab56' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 59149\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 36390</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"7816b146-741c-4de1-ba0e-8bd0e50b81c5","timestamp":"2026-04-23T04:43:09.442Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are a plan document reviewer. Verify this implementation plan is complete and ready for a skilled Go developer to execute step by step.\n\n**Plan to review:** /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/2026-04-22-entire-recap-visual-redesign-plan.md\n\n**Spec for reference:** /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/2026-04-22-entire-recap-visual-redesign-design.md\n\nThe plan is organized into 8 chunks (plus a prerequisite and final verification). Each chunk is logically self-contained and ends with a green commit.\n\n## What to Check\n\n| Category | What to Look For |\n|----------|------------------|\n| Completeness | TODOs, placeholders, incomplete tasks, missing steps |\n| Spec Alignment | Chunks cover all spec requirements, no scope creep |\n| Tas