rate limiting — does `/me/recap`? Worth a quick grep of the middleware stack if rate limits matter for cost control.\n\n**5. Cache invalidation.** The CLI's local enrichment cache at `.git/recap-analysis-cache/` invalidates on `pipeline_version` bumps. That's fine for per-checkpoint analyses but `/me/recap` itself isn't cached by the CLI. Each TUI open hits the endpoint. Probably fine for v1, could add caching later.\n\n**6. `--30` was removed in the CLI but `Range30d` still exists elsewhere?** Quick check — we removed it from the enum and all references. ✅ Already verified.\n\n**7. Server-side `recap_checkpoint_analyses` table.** In dev, that table didn't exist in `init-test-db.sql`. If prod is fine (I believe it is, since PlanetScale has it via live migrations), no action. If an internal reviewer's dev env lacks it, they'll hit 500s when testing locally.\n\n## What I'm NOT worried about\n\n- Frontend consumer: the regenerated SDK is there, any web dashboard can call `/me/recap` via the typed client\n- User data scoping: handler uses `userId` from the token throughout, no cross-user leak risk\n- Empty state handling: `{agents: {}, contributors: null}` renders cleanly in the CLI\n- Older CLI versions: they'll keep working — the legacy three-endpoint routes on the server aren't removed\n\n## Action I'd take now\n\n1. Flip server #1604 draft → ready (CI's green, mergeable)\n2. Request review\n3. After merge + deploy, flip CLI #1015 draft → ready\n4. Note the deploy order in both PRs so reviewers know\n\nWant me to flip #1604 to ready?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1579,"cache_read_input_tokens":676367,"output_tokens":3089,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1579,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3089,"cache_rea